    (78, E'svc-09', E'DNA Cloning service', E'Professional DNA cloning services for your research needs.', E'/media/product_images/99fa2ec1-247f-49fd-af65-7b2a3dbf64e1.png', E'/services/dna-cloning-service', E'synthesis-cloning', E'', E'service', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'', E'In Stock', E'', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/99fa2ec1-247f-49fd-af65-7b2a3dbf64e1.png']::text[], E'', E'', FALSE, NULL, E'{"link": "/services/dna-cloning-service", "name": "DNA Cloning service", "order": 0, "category": "synthesis-cloning", "imageUrl": "/media/product_images/99fa2ec1-247f-49fd-af65-7b2a3dbf64e1.png", "markdown": "", "caseStudies": [], "description": "Professional DNA cloning services for your research needs.", "keyBenefits": ["Expert cloning services", "Fast turnaround times", "High-quality results"], "longDescription": "Comprehensive DNA cloning services tailored to your research requirements.", "processOverview": [{"step": "Consultation", "description": "Discuss your DNA cloning requirements."}, {"step": "Design & Cloning", "description": "Vector design and DNA cloning."}, {"step": "Validation", "description": "Quality control and validation."}, {"step": "Delivery", "description": "Delivery with documentation."}], "relatedProducts": [], "showInHomepageServices": false}'::jsonb, NULL, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00'),
    (79, E'svc-custom-1766633756918', E'Virus Packaging Overview', E'Comprehensive viral packaging services, including AAV, Lentivirus, Retroviral (MLV), and Adenovirus systems.', E'/media/product_images/ff457910-f5b0-44b4-bcbc-920a8f51aa77.png', E'/services/virus-packaging-overview', E'virus-packaging', E'Others', E'service', NULL, 1766633756918, '2025-12-24T22:35:56.918000+00:00', E'', E'In Stock', E'', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'High transduction efficiency with low cytotoxicity', E'Batch-to-batch consistency and comprehensive QC', E'Optional functional assays for tagged/untagged proteins', E'Broad serotype variety and flexible vector design options']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/ff457910-f5b0-44b4-bcbc-920a8f51aa77.png']::text[], E'', E'At **BioArk Technologies**, we provide **end-to-end viral packaging services** encompassing **AAV**, **Lentivirus**, **Retrovirus (MLV)**, and **Adenovirus** systems.  
Each viral vector is produced as a **high-titer, ready-to-use formulation**, manufactured under **stringent quality control (QC)** pipelines and optionally validated through **functional assays** to ensure **outstanding performance**, **reproducibility**, and **reliability**.

Our **viral packaging platform** supports payload delivery for:
- **Gene expression**
- **RNA interference (knockdown)**
- **CRISPR/Cas-based genome editing**

We also offer **flexible vector design options**, including a variety of **promoters**, **tags**, **selection markers**, and **fluorescent reporters**, tailored to your experimental needs.

Our system is optimized to provide:
- ✅ **High transduction efficiency**
- ✅ **Low cytotoxicity**
- ✅ **Batch-to-batch consistency**
- ✅ **Broad host tropism** (effective in both dividing and non-dividing cells)

---

## Service Categories

### AAV Packaging Services
High-quality AAV packaging with ≥80% full particles, ≥95% purity, and guaranteed titers (≥1×10¹³ vg/mL) to support precise gene delivery and CRISPR applications.

### Lenti Packaging Services
High-titer, ready-to-use lentiviral vectors with full QC and optional functional testing for gene expression, knockdown, and CRISPR editing.

---

📩 **Contact:** [support@bioarktech.com](mailto:support@bioarktech.com)', FALSE, E'{"id": "svc-custom-1766633756918", "icon": "", "link": "/services/virus-packaging-overview", "name": "Virus Packaging Overview", "category": "virus-packaging", "imageUrl": "/media/product_images/ff457910-f5b0-44b4-bcbc-920a8f51aa77.png", "markdown": "At **BioArk Technologies**, we provide **end-to-end viral packaging services** encompassing **AAV**, **Lentivirus**, **Retrovirus (MLV)**, and **Adenovirus** systems.  \nEach viral vector is produced as a **high-titer, ready-to-use formulation**, manufactured under **stringent quality control (QC)** pipelines and optionally validated through **functional assays** to ensure **outstanding performance**, **reproducibility**, and **reliability**.\n\nOur **viral packaging platform** supports payload delivery for:\n- **Gene expression**\n- **RNA interference (knockdown)**\n- **CRISPR/Cas-based genome editing**\n\nWe also offer **flexible vector design options**, including a variety of **promoters**, **tags**, **selection markers**, and **fluorescent reporters**, tailored to your experimental needs.\n\nOur system is optimized to provide:\n- \u2705 **High transduction efficiency**\n- \u2705 **Low cytotoxicity**\n- \u2705 **Batch-to-batch consistency**\n- \u2705 **Broad host tropism** (effective in both dividing and non-dividing cells)\n\n---\n\n## Service Categories\n\n### AAV Packaging Services\nHigh-quality AAV packaging with \u226580% full particles, \u226595% purity, and guaranteed titers (\u22651\u00d710\u00b9\u00b3 vg/mL) to support precise gene delivery and CRISPR applications.\n\n### Lenti Packaging Services\nHigh-titer, ready-to-use lentiviral vectors with full QC and optional functional testing for gene expression, knockdown, and CRISPR editing.\n\n---\n\n\ud83d\udce9 **Contact:** [support@bioarktech.com](mailto:support@bioarktech.com)", "createdAt": 1766633756918, "groupName": "Others", "caseStudies": [], "description": "Comprehensive viral packaging services, including AAV, Lentivirus, Retroviral (MLV), and Adenovirus systems.", "keyBenefits": ["High transduction efficiency with low cytotoxicity", "Batch-to-batch consistency and comprehensive QC", "Optional functional assays for tagged/untagged proteins", "Broad serotype variety and flexible vector design options"], "longDescription": "We offer comprehensive viral packaging services, including AAV, Lentivirus, Retroviral (MLV), and Adenovirus systems. Each high-titer, ready-to-use viral particle is produced under stringent quality control (QC) standards and can be supplemented with optional functional testing to ensure exceptional performance and reliability.", "processOverview": [{"step": "System Selection", "description": "Choose the optimal viral system (AAV, Lentivirus, Retrovirus, or Adenovirus) for your application."}, {"step": "Vector Design", "description": "Customize promoters, tags, selection markers, and fluorescent reporters."}, {"step": "Packaging & QC", "description": "Optimized production with titer, purity, and functionality checks."}, {"step": "Delivery", "description": "Shipped on dry ice with comprehensive documentation."}], "relatedProducts": [], "showInHomepageServices": true}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00'),
    (80, E'svc-05', E'Cell Line Services', E'From vector design to monoclonal selection, validation, and banking.', E'/media/product_images/0a5f4fe1-7860-4f0b-8eba-2b3235da7392.jpg', E'/services/cell-line-generation', E'cell-line-services', E'', E'service', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'', E'In Stock', E'', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/0a5f4fe1-7860-4f0b-8eba-2b3235da7392.jpg']::text[], E'', E'', FALSE, NULL, E'{"link": "/services/cell-line-generation", "name": "Cell Line Services", "category": "cell-line-services", "imageUrl": "/media/product_images/0a5f4fe1-7860-4f0b-8eba-2b3235da7392.jpg", "markdown": "\nAt **BioArk Technologies**, we specialize in constructing **stable cell lines** tailored to meet your specific research needs.  \nWhether you\u2019re working with **cancer cell lines** or **adherent cell lines**, we offer a range of services including **gene overexpression**, **knockout**, **knock-in**, and **deletion**.  \n\nOur **affordable**, **reliable**, and **high-quality solutions** accelerate your research and deliver the results you need.  \nPartner with us to drive innovation in your projects today!\n\n---\n\n## Service Content\n\n## 1. Vector Construction\nWe offer comprehensive **design and construction of plasmid vectors** tailored to your genetic modification needs, with selectable markers for efficient screening.  \n\nOur vector construction services include:\n- **Gene Overexpression**\n- **Targeted Gene Overexpression** at *AAVS1* or other safe harbor sites  \n- **Inducible Gene Overexpression**\n- **Gene Knockout** via **CRISPR**\n- **Gene Deletion** using double **CRISPR cut sites**\n- **Gene Tagging Services**\n\n---\n\n## 2. Cell Line Transfection\nWe provide various **transfection methods** to suit different cell types and experimental requirements, including:\n- **Lipofection** \u2013 ideal for adherent cells  \n- **Electroporation** \u2013 for difficult-to-transfect cell types  \n- **Viral Transduction** \u2013 leveraging **lentiviruses** or **AAVs** to efficiently deliver genetic material into target cells  \n\n---\n\n## 3. Cell Line Pool\nOur services include the **development of stable cell lines**, customized to meet the unique needs of your project.  \nWe work with a wide variety of cell types, ensuring **functional characteristics** that align with your research goals.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Selection and Expansion\nWe apply **selective pressure**, such as **antibiotic selection**, to isolate successfully transfected cells.  \nSelected clones are **expanded in controlled environments** to ensure **consistency** and **stability**.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Validation of Stable Cell Lines\nWe provide **thorough characterization** of generated cell lines, including:\n\n- **Genomic Analysis**: Verification of gene integration through **PCR** or **sequencing**  \n- **Expression Analysis**: Evaluation of target gene expression using techniques such as **qPCR**, **Western blotting**, or **flow cytometry**\n", "caseStudies": [], "description": "From vector design to monoclonal selection, validation, and banking.", "keyBenefits": ["Guaranteed expression levels", "Comprehensive validation and QC reports", "Royalty-free for commercial use", "Fast turnaround times"], "longDescription": "Comprehensive stable cell line generation from vector design and construction to fully validated monoclonal cell lines.", "processOverview": [{"step": "Consultation & Design", "description": "Optimal vector design for your gene of interest."}, {"step": "Transfection & Selection", "description": "High-efficiency delivery followed by antibiotic/metabolic selection."}, {"step": "Monoclonal Isolation", "description": "Single-cell cloning via limiting dilution or FACS."}, {"step": "Validation & Banking", "description": "Expression/stability validation and cell banking."}], "relatedProducts": [], "showInHomepageServices": true}'::jsonb, NULL, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00'),
    (81, E'svc-02', E'Genome Editing Services', E'CRISPR overexpression, knockout, RNA knockdown, and ready-to-use kits for streamlined editing.', E'/media/product_images/4bbb795d-8216-4baa-8755-6a15aad7a6e5.jpeg', E'/services/genome-editing', E'genome-editing-service', E'', E'service', 20, NULL, NULL, E'', E'In Stock', E'', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/4bbb795d-8216-4baa-8755-6a15aad7a6e5.jpeg']::text[], E'', E'', FALSE, NULL, E'{"link": "/services/genome-editing", "name": "Genome Editing Services", "order": 20, "category": "genome-editing-service", "imageUrl": "/media/product_images/4bbb795d-8216-4baa-8755-6a15aad7a6e5.jpeg", "markdown": "## Targeted Overexpression with CRISPR\nOur targeted overexpression service allows for the precise and controlled expression of your gene of interest at specific genomic loci, including safe harbor sites like AAVS1. Compared with Lentivirus induced overexpression, targeted overexpression can provide more precision regulation and more safety and controllable knock-in effects. This service is ideal for:\n\n- Inducible or constitutive overexpression of target genes\n- Ensuring high-level, stable expression in your cell line\n- Requiring more accurate regulations, including inducible promoters.\n\n## CRISPR Knock-Out\nWe employ an optimized CRISPR-Cas9 system along with precisely designed guide RNAs (gRNAs) to achieve high knockout efficiency in both adherent and cancer cell lines. Our tailored knockout strategies are customized to meet your specific experimental requirements, ensuring reliable and reproducible results. Our services target a broad range of genomic loci, from exonic regions to safe harbor sites, minimizing off-target effects. We also provide thorough validation of knockout efficiency through genomic and expression analyses, including PCR, sequencing, and Western blotting.\n\n**Available in two formats:** lentivirus and standard plasmids  \n**Custom-designed guide RNAs (gRNAs)** for maximum knockout efficiency  \n**Ideal for** functional genomics and pathway analysis\n\n## CRISPR RNA Knockdown\nWe offer CRISPR-based RNA knockdown services that specifically target and degrade RNA transcripts, effectively reducing the expression of your gene of interest at the transcriptional level. Compared to traditional RNA interference (RNAi), CRISPR RNA technologies generally provide more efficient knockdown and greater target specificity.\n\n- Efficient RNA degradation using CRISPR/Cas13 technology\n- Ideal for high-throughput screening and gene function analysis\n- Offers a more dynamic and precise approach to gene silencing than conventional methods\n\n## Genome Editing Kits\n\n### Targeted Overexpression Plasmid Kit\n\nCatalog: (CDS-P011k) \u2014 $899 \u2014 2\u20133 weeks\n\nTransform your research with our innovative tool to integrate your interest genes into the safe harbor site AAVS1. Our targeted overexpression kit is optimized for use in various cancer cell lines, achieving a remarkable success rate in establishing stable cell lines.\n\n**Your Success is Our Commitment!**  \nWe guarantee that our kit will successfully generate stable overexpression clones in your transfectable cell lines. If it doesn\u2019t work, you\u2019ll receive a full refund.\n\nFor additional services related to stable cell lines, please reach out to us at support@BioArkTech.com.\n\n### CRISPR Knock-Out Plasmid Kit\n\nCatalog: (COT-P031k) \u2014 $790 \u2014 2\u20133 weeks\n\nOur knockout kit offers a fast and efficient solution to disrupt target genes in various cell lines, facilitating the creation of stable cell lines. It includes three all-in-one plasmids featuring optimized Cas9, gRNA structures, and selection markers for improved gene knockout efficiency.\n\n**Guaranteed Success!**  \nWe guarantee that our kit will successfully generate stable knockout clones in your transfectable cell lines. If it doesn\u2019t work, you\u2019ll receive a full refund.\n\nFor additional services related to stable cell lines, please get in touch with us at support@BioArkTech.com.\n\n### CRISPR Knock-Out Lentivirus Kit\n\nCatalog: (COM-P032k) \u2014 $1,499 \u2014 2\u20133 weeks\n\nOur knockout lentivirus kit harnesses advanced lentivirus technology to deliver all-in-one CRISPR knockout functional cassettes, expanding your applications across a broader range of cell lines. The kit includes a single tube of virus with three mixed gRNA sequences, streamlining your experimental process.\n\n**Guaranteed Results!**  \nWe guarantee that our kit will successfully generate stable knockout clones in your transfectable cell lines. If it doesn\u2019t work, you\u2019ll receive a full refund.\n\nFor additional services related to stable cell lines, please contact us at support@BioArkTech.com.\n\n### CRISPR RNA Knock-Down Plasmid Kit\n\nCatalog: (CRT-P051k) \u2014 $790 \u2014 2\u20133 weeks\n\nOur CRISPR RNA knockdown kits offer a highly specific and powerful alternative to traditional RNAi methods for reducing RNA expression levels. Achieve effective inhibition of target gene RNA levels by over 70% across a wide range of applications.\n\n**Guaranteed Efficiency!**  \nWe stand by our promise: our kit will efficiently inhibit your target genes in transfectable cell lines. If it doesn\u2019t work, you\u2019ll receive a full refund.\n\nFor any inquiries, please contact us at support@BioArkTech.com.\n", "caseStudies": [], "description": "CRISPR overexpression, knockout, RNA knockdown, and ready-to-use kits for streamlined editing.", "keyBenefits": ["Precise knock-in at safe harbor or locus-specific sites", "High-efficiency CRISPR knock-out with minimized off-targets", "CRISPR-based RNA knockdown for superior specificity", "Kits with success guarantee and rapid turnaround"], "longDescription": "Comprehensive genome editing solutions including targeted overexpression, CRISPR knock-out, RNA knockdown, and turnkey kits with delivery options.", "processOverview": [{"step": "Consultation", "description": "Discuss goals, targets, and editing strategy (overexpression/KO/RNA KD)."}, {"step": "Design", "description": "gRNA, donor template, and vector design optimized for your cell line."}, {"step": "Build & QC", "description": "Construct assembly, validation, and functional checks."}, {"step": "Delivery", "description": "Plasmid or lentivirus delivery with documentation and support."}], "relatedProducts": [], "showInHomepageServices": true}'::jsonb, NULL, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00'),
    (82, E'svc-04', E'Virus Packaging Services', E'Comprehensive viral packaging services, including AAV, Lentivirus, Retroviral (MLV), and Adenovirus systems. ', E'/media/product_images/e7c6e326-1cc0-4a5f-8336-336566725970.png', E'/services/virus-packaging-services', E'virus-packaging', E'', E'service', NULL, NULL, NULL, E'', E'In Stock', E'', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/e7c6e326-1cc0-4a5f-8336-336566725970.png']::text[], E'', E'', FALSE, NULL, E'{"link": "/services/virus-packaging-services", "name": "Virus Packaging Services", "hidden": true, "category": "virus-packaging", "imageUrl": "/media/product_images/e7c6e326-1cc0-4a5f-8336-336566725970.png", "markdown": "\nAt **BioArk Technologies**, we provide **end-to-end viral packaging services** encompassing **AAV**, **Lentivirus**, **Retrovirus (MLV)**, and **Adenovirus** systems.  \nEach viral vector is produced as a **high-titer, ready-to-use formulation**, manufactured under **stringent quality control (QC)** pipelines and optionally validated through **functional assays** to ensure **outstanding performance**, **reproducibility**, and **reliability**.\n\nOur **viral packaging platform** supports payload delivery for:\n- **Gene expression**\n- **RNA interference (knockdown)**\n- **CRISPR/Cas-based genome editing**\n\nWe also offer **flexible vector design options**, including a variety of **promoters**, **tags**, **selection markers**, and **fluorescent reporters**, tailored to your experimental needs.\n\nOur system is optimized to provide:\n- \u2705 **High transduction efficiency**\n- \u2705 **Low cytotoxicity**\n- \u2705 **Batch-to-batch consistency**\n- \u2705 **Broad host tropism** (effective in both dividing and non-dividing cells)\n\n---\n\n## Comparative Overview\n\n|               | **Lentivirus** | **Retrovirus** | **Adenovirus** | **AAV** |\n|---------------|----------------|----------------|----------------|----------|\n| **Tropism** | Broad | Broad | Broad (Ad5 serotype) | Serotype-dependent |\n| **Packaging Size** | ~8\u20139 kb | ~8 kb | ~36 kb | ~4.7 kb |\n| **Can Infect Non-dividing Cells?** | Yes | No | Yes | Yes |\n| **Stable Integration or Transient** | Stable integration | Stable integration | Transient (episomal) | Transient (episomal) |\n| **Maximum Titer** | High | Moderate | High | Very High |\n| **Promoter Customization** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n\n---\n\n## Technology Background\n\n## 1. Lentivirus\n\nLentiviral vectors are **second or third-generation systems** engineered for **high safety**, **efficient gene delivery**, and **broad host tropism**.\n\n### Key Features\n- **VSV-G pseudotyping** enables transduction across a wide range of cell types  \n- **Stable genomic integration** ensures long-term and heritable transgene expression  \n- Fully compatible with **CRISPR/Cas9**, **CRISPRa/i**, **shRNA**, and other functional constructs  \n\n### Applications\n- Stable **overexpression** or **knockdown** cell line generation  \n- **CRISPR-based** gene editing (knockout, activation, interference)  \n- **Pooled functional genomic screening**  \n- **Cell therapy research** and **ex vivo modification**\n\n---\n\n## 2. AAV (Adeno-Associated Virus)\n\nAAV vectors are **non-pathogenic**, **non-enveloped**, and **replication-incompetent**, making them among the **safest** and most **efficient** vectors for **in vivo gene delivery**.\n\n### Key Features\n- **Broad serotype diversity** *(AAV2, AAV5, AAV8, and over 40 additional options)* enabling **tissue-specific tropism**  \n- Supports **long-term, stable expression** in **post-mitotic** and **non-dividing cells**  \n- Exhibits **low immunogenicity** with **minimal genomic integration** *(predominantly episomal)*  \n- Manufactured with **high purity** and **low endotoxin levels**, suitable for **in vivo applications**\n\n### Applications\n- **In vivo gene therapy** and **targeted delivery**  \n- **Neuroscience**, **cardiovascular**, and **ocular** research  \n- **CRISPR-mediated in vivo editing**  \n- **Reporter expression**, **optogenetic modulation**, and **cell lineage tracing**\n\n---\n\n## 3. Retroviral (MLV) System\n\n**Murine Leukemia Virus (MLV)**-based retroviral vectors are well-established tools for **stable gene integration** in **actively dividing cells**.\n\n### Key Features\n- **Efficient genomic integration**, enabling **stable transgene expression** in proliferating cells  \n- Widely used for **hematopoietic**, **stem cell**, and **immune cell** modification  \n- Available in **ecotropic**, **amphotropic**, and **pantropic pseudotypes** for tailored host range  \n- Suitable for **gene overexpression**, **shRNA knockdown**, and **functional studies**\n\n### Applications\n- **Stable cell line generation** in dividing cell populations  \n- **Genetic modification** of stem or cancer cells  \n- **Functional genomics** and **screening studies**\n\n> **Note:** Retroviral vectors are limited to **dividing cells** and are **not effective** for non-dividing cell populations.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Adenovirus\n\nAdenoviral vectors are **non-integrating**, **high-capacity vectors** ideal for **transient**, **high-level gene expression** across a **broad spectrum of cell types**, including **non-dividing cells**.\n\n### Key Features\n- **Large payload capacity (~36 kb)** for complex transgene cassettes  \n- Enables **robust**, **transient transgene expression**  \n- **Non-integrating**, minimizing risk of **insertional mutagenesis**  \n- Broad tropism across **human** and **animal cell types**\n\n### Applications\n- **Short-term overexpression** and **reporter assays**  \n- **Vaccine** and **immunotherapy** development  \n- **Gene delivery** to non-dividing cells  \n- **Preclinical studies** requiring transient, high-level expression  \n\n---\n\n## Price Policy\n\n## Lentivirus Package Services\n\n| Catalog Number | Minimum Titer | Volume | 1st Tube Price | 2nd Tube Price | Turnaround |\n|----------------|----------------|--------|----------------|----------------|-------------|\n| **LPSVC-mini** | >10\u2077 TU/ml | 200 \u00b5l | $199 | Free / $199 | 2\u20133 weeks |\n| **LPSVC-midi** | >10\u2078 TU/ml | 200 \u00b5l | $399 | Free / $399 | 2\u20133 weeks |\n| **LPSVC-maxi** | >10\u2079 TU/ml | 200 \u00b5l | $699 | Free / $699 | 2\u20133 weeks |\n\n---\n\n## AAV Package Services\n\n| Catalog Number | Scale | Titer | Volume | Price | Turnaround |\n|----------------|--------|--------|---------|--------|-------------|\n| **AAVPS-1e12 vg** | 1e12 vg | >1e13 vg/ml | 1 \u00d7 100 \u00b5l | $1,100 ($1,200) | 2\u20133 weeks |\n| **AAVPS-5e12 vg** | 5e12 vg | >1e13 vg/ml | 2 \u00d7 250 \u00b5l | $1,390 ($1,600) | 2\u20133 weeks |\n| **AAVPS-1e13 vg** | 1e13 vg | >1e13 vg/ml | 2 \u00d7 500 \u00b5l | $2,080 ($2,300) | 2\u20133 weeks |\n| **AAVPS-5e13 vg** | 5e13 vg | >1e13 vg/ml | 5 \u00d7 1,000 \u00b5l | $6,780 ($7,600) | 2\u20133 weeks |\n| **AAVPS-1e14 vg** | 1e14 vg | >1e13 vg/ml | 10 \u00d7 1,000 \u00b5l | $10,260 ($11,600) | 2\u20133 weeks |\n\n---\n\n## Retrovirus (MLV) Package Services\n\n> *(Details Coming Soon)*\n\n---\n\n## Adenovirus Package Services\n\n> *(Details Coming Soon)*\n\n---\n\n\ud83d\udce9 **Contact:** [support@bioarktech.com](mailto:support@bioarktech.com)\n", "caseStudies": [], "description": "Comprehensive viral packaging services, including AAV, Lentivirus, Retroviral (MLV), and Adenovirus systems. ", "keyBenefits": ["High transduction efficiency with low cytotoxicity", "Batch-to-batch consistency and comprehensive QC", "Optional functional assays for tagged/untagged proteins"], "longDescription": "We offer comprehensive viral packaging services, including AAV, Lentivirus, Retroviral (MLV), and Adenovirus systems. Each high-titer, ready-to-use viral particle is produced under stringent quality control (QC) standards and can be supplemented with optional functional testing to ensure exceptional performance and reliability.", "processOverview": [{"step": "System Selection", "description": "Choose 2nd-gen (3-plasmid) or 3rd-gen (4-plasmid) systems."}, {"step": "Subcloning", "description": "MiniGFP (~330 bp) tags or selection markers (Puro/BSD/Neo, etc.)."}, {"step": "Packaging & QC", "description": "Optimized production with titer, purity, and functionality checks."}, {"step": "Delivery", "description": "Shipped on dry ice with documentation."}], "relatedProducts": [], "showInHomepageServices": true}'::jsonb, NULL, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00'),
    (83, E'svc-custom-1759768141509', E'Lentivirus Packaging Services', E'High-titer, ready-to-use lentiviral vectors with full QC and optional functional testing.', NULL, E'/services/lentivirus-packaging-services', E'virus-packaging', E'', E'service', NULL, 1759768141509, '2025-10-06T11:29:01.509000+00:00', E'', E'In Stock', E'', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'High transduction efficiency with low cytotoxicity', E'Batch-to-batch consistency and comprehensive QC', E'Optional functional assays for tagged/untagged proteins']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], E'', E'### Technology Background
**2nd Generation (Three-Plasmid):** Transfer, Packaging (Gag/Pol/Rev), Envelope.  
**3rd Generation (Four-Plasmid):** Transfer, Gag/Pol, Rev, Envelope — safer but typically lower titer (default).

### Service Offerings
1. Project Support — System selection and construct customization.  
2. Lentivirus Subcloning — MiniGFP (~330 bp) or selection markers (Puro/BSD/Neo, custom).  
3. Lentivirus Packaging — Optimized yield and purity; full QC.  
4. Functional Testing — qPCR, fluorescence, immunofluorescence, Western blot (custom).

### Pricing
| Catalog Number | Minimum Titer | Volume | 1st Tube Price | 2nd Tube Price | Turnaround |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| LPSVC-mini | >10^7 TU/ml | 200 µl | $199 | $199 | 2–3 weeks |
| LPSVC-midi | >10^8 TU/ml | 200 µl | $399 | $399 | 2–3 weeks |
| LPSVC-maxi | >10^9 TU/ml | 200 µl | $699 | $699 | 2–3 weeks |

### Functional Services (Add-ons)
| Titer and Functional Service | Price | Note |
| --- | --- | --- |
| qPCR | - | Optimized RT‑qPCR quantifies lentiviral RNA |
| Fluorescent Tag Analysis | +$50 | HEK293T infection and imaging (GFP/RFP/BFP, etc.) |
| Protein Tag Analysis (IF) | +$70 | Immunofluorescence for Myc/His/Flag or custom tags |
| Customized Testing (WB) | +$120 | Western blot; customer provides primary antibody |

### Subcloning & Analysis
| Service | Price | Note |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Lenti‑miniGFP Subcloning & Fluorescence | +$199 | Transfer gene to miniGFP construct; HEK293T infection/analysis |
| Lenti Selection Subcloning | +$189 | Transfer to selection constructs (Puro/BSD/Neo or custom) |

Contact: support@bioarktech.com
