manufactured from high-quality polypropylene (PP) to provide reliable performance, precision liquid handling, and enhanced sample protection for a wide range of laboratory workflows. Designed for both single-channel and multi-channel pipettes, these tips offer broad compatibility with most major pipette brands, including Eppendorf, Gilson, Thermo Fisher, Sartorius, Biohit, Oxford, DLAB, and other standard pipette systems.\\n\\nFeaturing an integrated aerosol barrier filter and low-retention surface technology, these tips help minimize the risk of cross-contamination, liquid backflow, and pipette contamination while maximizing sample recovery. The low-retention design reduces liquid adhesion, improving pipetting accuracy and consistency, particularly when working with valuable or low-volume samples.\\n\\nAs one of the most widely used pipette tip formats in research, clinical, and diagnostic laboratories, these universal filtered tips provide a cost-effective solution for routine liquid handling applications while maintaining high standards of quality and performance. Please note that Rainin pipettes require specially designed tips and are not compatible with standard universal pipette tips. Users of less common pipette brands are encouraged to verify compatibility prior to purchase."}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/bb285c11-92d7-4b8a-89d9-eb706f278b79.webp", "/media/product_images/ab51e8f1-f437-4128-9f53-851656e67228.webp", "/media/product_images/362b2dd2-11ab-4020-a0b1-b8028bcafd6c.webp", "/media/product_images/71b2ded9-f76d-4e59-a492-6f4c9278350f.webp", "/media/product_images/43a940cb-f20d-4c74-b19a-0bd2d0494fe1.webp"], "manuals": [], "options": ["10 Racks/Box; 5 Boxes/Case"], "createdAt": 1780975995260, "listPrice": "$280", "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "isFeatured": false, "manualUrls": [], "keyFeatures": ["\\u2022 Low-Retention Surface for Enhanced Sample Recovery and Pipetting Accuracy", "\\u2022 Integrated Aerosol Barrier Filter Helps Prevent Cross-Contamination and Liquid Backflow", "\\u2022 Universal Compatibility with Most Major Single- and Multi-Channel Pipettes", "\\u2022 Manufactured in a Class 100,000 Cleanroom Environment", "\\u2022 Certified DNase-Free, RNase-Free, and Non-Pyrogenic", "\\u2022 Sterile and Ready-to-Use for Sensitive Laboratory Applications", "\\u2022 CE Marked and ISO 13485:2016 Certified", "\\u2022 Compliant with IVDD 98/79/EC Requirements", "\\u2022 Consistent Quality and Reliable Performance for Routine and Precision Liquid Handling", "\\u2022 Ideal for PCR, qPCR, Molecular Biology, Cell Culture, and Diagnostic Workflows"], "availability": "In Stock", "optionPrices": {}, "catalogNumber": "800509-S", "performanceData": "\\u2022 Accurate Liquid Transfer and Precision Pipetting\\n\\n\\u2022 Reagent, Buffer, and Sample Preparation\\n\\n\\u2022 PCR, qPCR, and Nucleic Acid Workflows\\n\\n\\u2022 Sample Dispensing into Microplates, PCR Plates, and Reaction Tubes\\n\\n\\u2022 Cell Culture and Microbiology Applications\\n\\n\\u2022 Electrophoresis Gel Loading\\n\\n\\u2022 ELISA and Diagnostic Assays\\n\\n\\u2022 Supernatant Transfer and Phase Separation Procedures\\n\\n\\u2022 High-Throughput Screening and Automated Liquid Handling\\n\\n\\u2022 Routine Research, Clinical, and Analytical Laboratory Operations", "storageStability": "", "showInReagentSection": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00'),
    (53, E'custom-1780977833573', E'25 mL Individually Wrapped Serological Pipette, Filtered', E'BioArk 25 mL Polystyrene Sterile Serological Pipettes are designed to provide accurate liquid measurement and transfer for a wide range of laboratory applications. Manufactured from high-clarity polystyrene, these disposable pipettes offer excellent visibility for precise volume reading and reliable performance in cell culture, molecular biology, microbiology, clinical diagnostics, and pharmaceutical research. Their precision-molded construction ensures consistent liquid handling and dependable results across routine laboratory workflows.\n\nEach pipette is individually wrapped and sterilized by gamma irradiation or E-beam processing to maintain sterility and support aseptic techniques. Certified RNase-free, DNase-free, and non-pyrogenic, these pipettes help minimize the risk of sample contamination, making them suitable for sensitive biological and diagnostic applications. Clear, bidirectional graduations and highly visible color-coded markings enable fast volume identification and accurate dispensing, improving workflow efficiency and user convenience.\n\nDesigned for seamless compatibility with most standard pipette controllers and pipette aids, Biofargo serological pipettes provide a convenient, cost-effective solution for daily laboratory liquid handling. Their combination of accuracy, sterility, and ease of use makes them an ideal choice for research, clinical, and industrial laboratory environments.', E'/media/product_images/fddb37f7-c05a-42aa-a6ab-3f4675b7b62a.webp', E'/reagents/25-ml-individually-wrapped-serological-pipette-filtered', E'category-1780539818236', E'Serological Pipettes', E'product', NULL, 1780977833573, '2026-06-08T23:03:53.573000+00:00', E'BA804025', E'In Stock', E'$385', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'• Sterile and Ready for Immediate Use – Individually packaged and sterilized by E-beam or gamma irradiation to ensure aseptic handling and minimize contamination risk.', E'• Precise Liquid Measurement and Transfer – Calibrated 2 mL capacity with clear, bidirectional graduations for accurate aspiration and dispensing.', E'• Premium Virgin Polystyrene Construction – Manufactured from high-clarity polystyrene for excellent transparency, reliable performance, and enhanced chemical resistance.', E'• Certified Free of Biological Contaminants – RNase-free, DNase-free, non-pyrogenic, and non-cytotoxic, making the pipettes suitable for sensitive research and diagnostic applications.', E'• Easy Volume Identification – Distinctive color-coded markings enable rapid size recognition and improve laboratory workflow efficiency.', E'• Broad Instrument Compatibility – Designed to fit most standard pipette controllers and pipette aids commonly used in research, clinical, and industrial laboratories.', E'• Single-Use Disposable Design – Eliminates cleaning requirements and helps reduce sample carryover, cross-contamination, and experimental variability.', E'• Optimized for Laboratory Workflows – Ideal for cell culture, microbiology, molecular biology, clinical diagnostics, and general liquid handling applications.']::text[], ARRAY[E'6 Packs/Case(600 Pcs/Case)']::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'• Cell Culture and Tissue Culture Workflows – Accurate transfer of culture media, buffers, reagents, and cell suspensions in routine cell-based applications.\n\n• Clinical and Diagnostic Testing – Reliable liquid handling for sample preparation, assay setup, and laboratory diagnostic procedures.\n\n• Biotechnology and Pharmaceutical Research – Suitable for drug discovery, bioprocess development, formulation studies, and other research applications.\n\n• Microbiology and Bacteriology Studies – Precise measurement and transfer of microbial cultures, growth media, and laboratory reagents.\n\n• Sample Preparation and Reagent Mixing – Efficient handling, dilution, mixing, and dispensing of biological and chemical solutions.\n\n• Molecular Biology and Life Science Research – Ideal for routine laboratory workflows involving nucleic acids, proteins, enzymes, and other biological samples.\n\n• Quality Control and Analytical Laboratories – Consistent liquid transfer for testing, validation, and quality assurance procedures across research and manufacturing environments.', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/fddb37f7-c05a-42aa-a6ab-3f4675b7b62a.webp', E'/media/product_images/3c4b820a-369d-4fe9-947b-0013569bace0.JPG', E'/media/product_images/70cfe8a3-95fa-4c2f-8f5c-4acfb8594e60.JPG', E'/media/product_images/1e9c3f67-6e7f-47ca-99e2-1590ce8a9806.JPG']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1780977833573", "link": "/reagents/25-ml-individually-wrapped-serological-pipette-filtered", "name": "25 mL Individually Wrapped Serological Pipette, Filtered", "category": "category-1780539818236", "imageUrl": "", "createdAt": 1780977833573, "groupName": "Serological Pipettes", "description": "BioArk 25 mL Polystyrene Sterile Serological Pipettes are designed to provide accurate liquid measurement and transfer for a wide range of laboratory applications. Manufactured from high-clarity polystyrene, these disposable pipettes offer excellent visibility for precise volume reading and reliable performance in cell culture, molecular biology, microbiology, clinical diagnostics, and pharmaceutical research. Their precision-molded construction ensures consistent liquid handling and dependable results across routine laboratory workflows.\\n\\nEach pipette is individually wrapped and sterilized by gamma irradiation or E-beam processing to maintain sterility and support aseptic techniques. Certified RNase-free, DNase-free, and non-pyrogenic, these pipettes help minimize the risk of sample contamination, making them suitable for sensitive biological and diagnostic applications. Clear, bidirectional graduations and highly visible color-coded markings enable fast volume identification and accurate dispensing, improving workflow efficiency and user convenience.\\n\\nDesigned for seamless compatibility with most standard pipette controllers and pipette aids, Biofargo serological pipettes provide a convenient, cost-effective solution for daily laboratory liquid handling. Their combination of accuracy, sterility, and ease of use makes them an ideal choice for research, clinical, and industrial laboratory environments."}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/fddb37f7-c05a-42aa-a6ab-3f4675b7b62a.webp", "/media/product_images/3c4b820a-369d-4fe9-947b-0013569bace0.JPG", "/media/product_images/70cfe8a3-95fa-4c2f-8f5c-4acfb8594e60.JPG", "/media/product_images/1e9c3f67-6e7f-47ca-99e2-1590ce8a9806.JPG"], "manuals": [], "options": ["6 Packs/Case(600 Pcs/Case)"], "createdAt": 1780977833573, "listPrice": "$385", "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "isFeatured": false, "manualUrls": [], "keyFeatures": ["\\u2022 Sterile and Ready for Immediate Use \\u2013 Individually packaged and sterilized by E-beam or gamma irradiation to ensure aseptic handling and minimize contamination risk.", "\\u2022 Precise Liquid Measurement and Transfer \\u2013 Calibrated 2 mL capacity with clear, bidirectional graduations for accurate aspiration and dispensing.", "\\u2022 Premium Virgin Polystyrene Construction \\u2013 Manufactured from high-clarity polystyrene for excellent transparency, reliable performance, and enhanced chemical resistance.", "\\u2022 Certified Free of Biological Contaminants \\u2013 RNase-free, DNase-free, non-pyrogenic, and non-cytotoxic, making the pipettes suitable for sensitive research and diagnostic applications.", "\\u2022 Easy Volume Identification \\u2013 Distinctive color-coded markings enable rapid size recognition and improve laboratory workflow efficiency.", "\\u2022 Broad Instrument Compatibility \\u2013 Designed to fit most standard pipette controllers and pipette aids commonly used in research, clinical, and industrial laboratories.", "\\u2022 Single-Use Disposable Design \\u2013 Eliminates cleaning requirements and helps reduce sample carryover, cross-contamination, and experimental variability.", "\\u2022 Optimized for Laboratory Workflows \\u2013 Ideal for cell culture, microbiology, molecular biology, clinical diagnostics, and general liquid handling applications."], "availability": "In Stock", "optionPrices": {}, "catalogNumber": "BA804025", "performanceData": "\\u2022 Cell Culture and Tissue Culture Workflows \\u2013 Accurate transfer of culture media, buffers, reagents, and cell suspensions in routine cell-based applications.\\n\\n\\u2022 Clinical and Diagnostic Testing \\u2013 Reliable liquid handling for sample preparation, assay setup, and laboratory diagnostic procedures.\\n\\n\\u2022 Biotechnology and Pharmaceutical Research \\u2013 Suitable for drug discovery, bioprocess development, formulation studies, and other research applications.\\n\\n\\u2022 Microbiology and Bacteriology Studies \\u2013 Precise measurement and transfer of microbial cultures, growth media, and laboratory reagents.\\n\\n\\u2022 Sample Preparation and Reagent Mixing \\u2013 Efficient handling, dilution, mixing, and dispensing of biological and chemical solutions.\\n\\n\\u2022 Molecular Biology and Life Science Research \\u2013 Ideal for routine laboratory workflows involving nucleic acids, proteins, enzymes, and other biological samples.\\n\\n\\u2022 Quality Control and Analytical Laboratories \\u2013 Consistent liquid transfer for testing, validation, and quality assurance procedures across research and manufacturing environments.", "storageStability": "", "showInReagentSection": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00'),
    (54, E'custom-1780979358256', E'Sterile Cell Spreaders (Individually or Bulk Packaged)', E'BioArk Sterile Cell Spreaders are designed for the uniform spreading of bacterial, yeast, and other microbial cultures across agar surfaces, ensuring consistent colony distribution and reliable experimental results. Manufactured from high-quality, smooth-finished plastic, these disposable spreaders provide gentle and even sample distribution without damaging the agar surface.\n\nThe ergonomic design enables comfortable handling and precise control, making them ideal for routine microbiology, environmental testing, food safety, clinical diagnostics, and life science research applications. The smooth spreading surface helps achieve uniform cell distribution, improving colony isolation and reproducibility across culture plates.\n\nAvailable in both individually wrapped sterile packaging and bulk-packaged sterile formats, BioArk Cell Spreaders offer flexibility to meet the needs of different laboratory workflows. Sterilized and ready to use, they eliminate the need for flaming or re-sterilization, reducing contamination risks and improving laboratory efficiency.', E'/media/product_images/f18620da-c319-4532-ab99-294b1bffdb50.webp', E'/reagents/sterile-cell-spreaders-individually-or-bulk-packaged', E'category-1780539818236', E'Bacterial Culture plate', E'product', NULL, 1780979358256, '2026-06-08T23:29:18.256000+00:00', E'BA651001', E'In Stock', E'$56', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'• Ideal for Uniform Spreading of Bacterial, Yeast, and Microbial Cultures', E'• Smooth, Polished Spreading Surface Minimizes Agar Damage During Use', E'• Slightly Angled Design Enhances Control and Promotes Even Sample Distribution', E'• L-Shaped Configuration Enables Complete Coverage of Petri Dish and Agar Plate Surfaces', E'• Disposable Design Eliminates the Need for Flaming or Re-Sterilization', E'• Gamma Irradiated and Sterile for Immediate Use', E'• Helps Reduce Cross-Contamination Risks in Microbiological Workflows', E'• Lightweight and Ergonomic for Comfortable Handling', E'• Available in Individually Wrapped or Bulk-Packaged Sterile Formats', E'• Suitable for Routine Microbiology, Environmental Testing, Clinical, and Research Applications']::text[], ARRAY[E'500 Pcs/Case']::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'• Facilitates the uniform spreading of bacterial, yeast, and fungal cultures on agar plates for colony isolation and enumeration.\n\n• Supports microbiological testing in research, clinical, environmental, food safety, and quality control laboratories.\n\n• Ideal for microbial plating, colony counting, and culture purity assessment procedures.\n\n• Enables efficient sample distribution for antimicrobial susceptibility testing and microbial screening workflows.\n\n• Suitable for environmental monitoring and contamination detection applications.\n\n• Supports routine microbiology, biotechnology, and life science research studies.\n\n• Provides consistent sample spreading for educational, academic, and teaching laboratory applications.', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/f18620da-c319-4532-ab99-294b1bffdb50.webp', E'/media/product_images/c09b1c09-c7cb-410c-834d-4a88e001de13.webp', E'/media/product_images/ea443066-b80a-4b16-8ec6-c211142c55ba.webp', E'/media/product_images/af1f069a-05e1-4649-9bbc-a37d714ca4dc.webp']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1780979358256", "link": "/reagents/sterile-cell-spreaders-individually-or-bulk-packaged", "name": "Sterile Cell Spreaders (Individually or Bulk Packaged)", "category": "category-1780539818236", "imageUrl": "", "createdAt": 1780979358256, "groupName": "Bacterial Culture plate", "description": "BioArk Sterile Cell Spreaders are designed for the uniform spreading of bacterial, yeast, and other microbial cultures across agar surfaces, ensuring consistent colony distribution and reliable experimental results. Manufactured from high-quality, smooth-finished plastic, these disposable spreaders provide gentle and even sample distribution without damaging the agar surface.\\n\\nThe ergonomic design enables comfortable handling and precise control, making them ideal for routine microbiology, environmental testing, food safety, clinical diagnostics, and life science research applications. The smooth spreading surface helps achieve uniform cell distribution, improving colony isolation and reproducibility across culture plates.\\n\\nAvailable in both individually wrapped sterile packaging and bulk-packaged sterile formats, BioArk Cell Spreaders offer flexibility to meet the needs of different laboratory workflows. Sterilized and ready to use, they eliminate the need for flaming or re-sterilization, reducing contamination risks and improving laboratory efficiency."}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/f18620da-c319-4532-ab99-294b1bffdb50.webp", "/media/product_images/c09b1c09-c7cb-410c-834d-4a88e001de13.webp", "/media/product_images/ea443066-b80a-4b16-8ec6-c211142c55ba.webp", "/media/product_images/af1f069a-05e1-4649-9bbc-a37d714ca4dc.webp"], "manuals": [], "options": ["500 Pcs/Case"], "createdAt": 1780979358256, "listPrice": "$56", "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "isFeatured": false, "manualUrls": [], "keyFeatures": ["\\u2022 Ideal for Uniform Spreading of Bacterial, Yeast, and Microbial Cultures", "\\u2022 Smooth, Polished Spreading Surface Minimizes Agar Damage During Use", "\\u2022 Slightly Angled Design Enhances Control and Promotes Even Sample Distribution", "\\u2022 L-Shaped Configuration Enables Complete Coverage of Petri Dish and Agar Plate Surfaces", "\\u2022 Disposable Design Eliminates the Need for Flaming or Re-Sterilization", "\\u2022 Gamma Irradiated and Sterile for Immediate Use", "\\u2022 Helps Reduce Cross-Contamination Risks in Microbiological Workflows", "\\u2022 Lightweight and Ergonomic for Comfortable Handling", "\\u2022 Available in Individually Wrapped or Bulk-Packaged Sterile Formats", "\\u2022 Suitable for Routine Microbiology, Environmental Testing, Clinical, and Research Applications"], "availability": "In Stock", "optionPrices": {}, "catalogNumber": "BA651001", "performanceData": "\\u2022 Facilitates the uniform spreading of bacterial, yeast, and fungal cultures on agar plates for colony isolation and enumeration.\\n\\n\\u2022 Supports microbiological testing in research, clinical, environmental, food safety, and quality control laboratories.\\n\\n\\u2022 Ideal for microbial plating, colony counting, and culture purity assessment procedures.\\n\\n\\u2022 Enables efficient sample distribution for antimicrobial susceptibility testing and microbial screening workflows.\\n\\n\\u2022 Suitable for environmental monitoring and contamination detection applications.\\n\\n\\u2022 Supports routine microbiology, biotechnology, and life science research studies.\\n\\n\\u2022 Provides consistent sample spreading for educational, academic, and teaching laboratory applications.", "storageStability": "", "showInReagentSection": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00'),
    (55, E'custom-1780980465967', E'35 mm Tissue Culture-Treated Cell Culture Dish, Sterile', E'BioArk 35 mm Cell Culture Dishes are manufactured from high-quality polystyrene and feature a tissue culture (TC)-treated surface to support optimal cell attachment, growth, and proliferation. Designed for routine cell culture applications, these dishes provide a reliable environment for cultivating a wide range of adherent cell types in research, biotechnology, and pharmaceutical laboratories.\n\nThe precision-engineered flat-bottom design creates a uniform growth surface, promoting even cell distribution and reducing variability caused by surface irregularities. This helps improve culture consistency, experimental reproducibility, and the accuracy of downstream analyses. The crystal-clear construction also allows excellent visibility for routine microscopic observation and cell monitoring.\n\nProduced under strict quality standards, BioArk cell culture dishes provide dependable performance for cell maintenance, expansion, transfection studies, and other cell-based research applications.', E'/media/product_images/b567418c-a95b-43b8-ac84-fbe1e8e2b4d5.png', E'/reagents/35-mm-tissue-culture-treated-cell-culture-dish-sterile', E'category-1780539818236', E'Cell Culture Dishes', E'product', NULL, 1780980465967, '2026-06-08T23:47:45.967000+00:00', E'BA803035', E'In Stock', E'$123', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'• Enhanced Handling and Ergonomic Design', E'• Secure and Stable Stacking for Easy Storage and Transport', E'• TC-Treated Surface for Improved Cell Attachment and Growth', E'• Suitable for Both Adherent and Suspension Cell Culture', E'• Uniform Growth Surface for Consistent Cell Distribution', E'• Excellent Optical Clarity for Microscopic Observation', E'• Ideal for Cell-Based Assays and Biological Research', E'• Reliable Performance for Routine Cell Culture Applications', E'• Durable Polystyrene Construction', E'• Sterile and Ready-to-Use']::text[], ARRAY[E'25 Packs/Case(500 Pcs/Case)']::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'• Supports the culture, expansion, and maintenance of adherent cells for routine research and laboratory applications.\n\n• Provides a suitable environment for the growth and handling of suspension cells in biological and biomedical studies.\n\n• Enables cell-based assays, including cell viability, proliferation, migration, and cytotoxicity studies.\n\n• Facilitates microscopic observation, cell imaging, and morphological analysis through its optically clear design.\n\n• Supports studies of cell signaling pathways, cellular responses, and cell-to-cell communication.\n\n• Ideal for stem cell and primary cell culture applications requiring reliable cell attachment and growth conditions.\n\n• Widely used in drug discovery, compound screening, and toxicity testing workflows.\n\n• Serves as a versatile platform for biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and life science research applications.\n\n• Promotes consistent and reproducible cell growth for downstream molecular and cellular analyses.', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/b567418c-a95b-43b8-ac84-fbe1e8e2b4d5.png', E'/media/product_images/18678a83-8740-47dc-ae41-186d98f483a2.png', E'/media/product_images/7fa634f7-8d7d-485f-b07f-4487f34d03a7.png', E'/media/product_images/c137b791-1bc8-4221-9dd8-7c0b31c30410.png']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1780980465967", "link": "/reagents/35-mm-tissue-culture-treated-cell-culture-dish-sterile", "name": "35 mm Tissue Culture-Treated Cell Culture Dish, Sterile", "category": "category-1780539818236", "imageUrl": "", "createdAt": 1780980465967, "groupName": "Cell Culture Dishes", "description": "BioArk 35 mm Cell Culture Dishes are manufactured from high-quality polystyrene and feature a tissue culture (TC)-treated surface to support optimal cell attachment, growth, and proliferation. Designed for routine cell culture applications, these dishes provide a reliable environment for cultivating a wide range of adherent cell types in research, biotechnology, and pharmaceutical laboratories.\\n\\nThe precision-engineered flat-bottom design creates a uniform growth surface, promoting even cell distribution and reducing variability caused by surface irregularities. This helps improve culture consistency, experimental reproducibility, and the accuracy of downstream analyses. The crystal-clear construction also allows excellent visibility for routine microscopic observation and cell monitoring.\\n\\nProduced under strict quality standards, BioArk cell culture dishes provide dependable performance for cell maintenance, expansion, transfection studies, and other cell-based research applications."}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/b567418c-a95b-43b8-ac84-fbe1e8e2b4d5.png", "/media/product_images/18678a83-8740-47dc-ae41-186d98f483a2.png", "/media/product_images/7fa634f7-8d7d-485f-b07f-4487f34d03a7.png", "/media/product_images/c137b791-1bc8-4221-9dd8-7c0b31c30410.png"], "manuals": [], "options": ["25 Packs/Case(500 Pcs/Case)"], "createdAt": 1780980465967, "listPrice": "$123", "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "isFeatured": false, "manualUrls": [], "keyFeatures": ["\\u2022 Enhanced Handling and Ergonomic Design", "\\u2022 Secure and Stable Stacking for Easy Storage and Transport", "\\u2022 TC-Treated Surface for Improved Cell Attachment and Growth", "\\u2022 Suitable for Both Adherent and Suspension Cell Culture", "\\u2022 Uniform Growth Surface for Consistent Cell Distribution", "\\u2022 Excellent Optical Clarity for Microscopic Observation", "\\u2022 Ideal for Cell-Based Assays and Biological Research", "\\u2022 Reliable Performance for Routine Cell Culture Applications", "\\u2022 Durable Polystyrene Construction", "\\u2022 Sterile and Ready-to-Use"], "availability": "In Stock", "optionPrices": {}, "catalogNumber": "BA803035", "performanceData": "\\u2022 Supports the culture, expansion, and maintenance of adherent cells for routine research and laboratory applications.\\n\\n\\u2022 Provides a suitable environment for the growth and handling of suspension cells in biological and biomedical studies.\\n\\n\\u2022 Enables cell-based assays, including cell viability, proliferation, migration, and cytotoxicity studies.\\n\\n\\u2022 Facilitates microscopic observation, cell imaging, and morphological analysis through its optically clear design.\\n\\n\\u2022 Supports studies of cell signaling pathways, cellular responses, and cell-to-cell communication.\\n\\n\\u2022 Ideal for stem cell and primary cell culture applications requiring reliable cell attachment and growth conditions.\\n\\n\\u2022 Widely used in drug discovery, compound screening, and toxicity testing workflows.\\n\\n\\u2022 Serves as a versatile platform for biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and life science research applications.\\n\\n\\u2022 Promotes consistent and reproducible cell growth for downstream molecular and cellular analyses.", "storageStability": "", "showInReagentSection": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896000+00:00'),
    (56, E'custom-1780977616154', E'10 mL Individually Wrapped Serological Pipette, Filtered', E'BioArk 10 mL Polystyrene Sterile Serological Pipettes are designed to provide accurate liquid measurement and transfer for a wide range of laboratory applications. Manufactured from high-clarity polystyrene, these disposable pipettes offer excellent visibility for precise volume reading and reliable performance in cell culture, molecular biology, microbiology, clinical diagnostics, and pharmaceutical research. Their precision-molded construction ensures consistent liquid handling and dependable results across routine laboratory workflows.\n\nEach pipette is individually wrapped and sterilized by gamma irradiation or E-beam processing to maintain sterility and support aseptic techniques. Certified RNase-free, DNase-free, and non-pyrogenic, these pipettes help minimize the risk of sample contamination, making them suitable for sensitive biological and diagnostic applications. Clear, bidirectional graduations and highly visible color-coded markings enable fast volume identification and accurate dispensing, improving workflow efficiency and user convenience.\n\nDesigned for seamless compatibility with most standard pipette controllers and pipette aids, Biofargo serological pipettes provide a convenient, cost-effective solution for daily laboratory liquid handling. Their combination of accuracy, sterility, and ease of use makes them an ideal choice for research, clinical, and industrial laboratory environments.', E'/media/product_images/35e2a40a-e9cb-40e7-8ca5-266747766cb6.webp', E'/reagents/10-ml-individually-wrapped-serological-pipette-filtered', E'category-1780539818236', E'Serological Pipettes', E'product', NULL, 1780977616154, '2026-06-08T23:00:16.154000+00:00', E'BA804010', E'In Stock', E'$350', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'• Sterile and Ready for Immediate Use – Individually packaged and sterilized by E-beam or gamma irradiation to ensure aseptic handling 