    (65, E'custom-1780980717391', E'150 mm Tissue Culture-Treated Cell Culture Dish, Sterile', E'BioArk 150 mm Cell Culture Dishes are manufactured from high-quality polystyrene and feature a tissue culture (TC)-treated surface to support optimal cell attachment, growth, and proliferation. Designed for routine cell culture applications, these dishes provide a reliable environment for cultivating a wide range of adherent cell types in research, biotechnology, and pharmaceutical laboratories.\n\nThe precision-engineered flat-bottom design creates a uniform growth surface, promoting even cell distribution and reducing variability caused by surface irregularities. This helps improve culture consistency, experimental reproducibility, and the accuracy of downstream analyses. The crystal-clear construction also allows excellent visibility for routine microscopic observation and cell monitoring.\n\nProduced under strict quality standards, BioArk cell culture dishes provide dependable performance for cell maintenance, expansion, transfection studies, and other cell-based research applications.', E'/media/product_images/87cd0436-5f9e-403b-8995-ce9d6d1eb723.jpg', E'/reagents/150-mm-tissue-culture-treated-cell-culture-dish-sterile', E'category-1780539818236', E'Cell Culture Dishes', E'product', NULL, 1780980717391, E'2026-06-08T23:51:57.391000', E'BA803150', E'In Stock', E'$141', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'• Enhanced Handling and Ergonomic Design', E'• Secure and Stable Stacking for Easy Storage and Transport', E'• TC-Treated Surface for Improved Cell Attachment and Growth', E'• Suitable for Both Adherent and Suspension Cell Culture', E'• Uniform Growth Surface for Consistent Cell Distribution', E'• Excellent Optical Clarity for Microscopic Observation', E'• Ideal for Cell-Based Assays and Biological Research', E'• Reliable Performance for Routine Cell Culture Applications', E'• Durable Polystyrene Construction', E'• Sterile and Ready-to-Use']::text[], ARRAY[E'8 Packs/Case(80 Pcs/Case)']::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'• Supports the culture, expansion, and maintenance of adherent cells for routine research and laboratory applications.\n\n• Provides a suitable environment for the growth and handling of suspension cells in biological and biomedical studies.\n\n• Enables cell-based assays, including cell viability, proliferation, migration, and cytotoxicity studies.\n\n• Facilitates microscopic observation, cell imaging, and morphological analysis through its optically clear design.\n\n• Supports studies of cell signaling pathways, cellular responses, and cell-to-cell communication.\n\n• Ideal for stem cell and primary cell culture applications requiring reliable cell attachment and growth conditions.\n\n• Widely used in drug discovery, compound screening, and toxicity testing workflows.\n\n• Serves as a versatile platform for biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and life science research applications.\n\n• Promotes consistent and reproducible cell growth for downstream molecular and cellular analyses.', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/87cd0436-5f9e-403b-8995-ce9d6d1eb723.jpg', E'/media/product_images/06b3841a-d637-442a-a973-638a79b75228.jpg', E'/media/product_images/33ce6789-ba0a-4fb9-998b-093f10295aaa.jpg', E'/media/product_images/192d411d-cdb9-40d9-a948-049a3b74da38.jpg']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1780980717391", "name": "150 mm Tissue Culture-Treated Cell Culture Dish, Sterile", "description": "BioArk 150 mm Cell Culture Dishes are manufactured from high-quality polystyrene and feature a tissue culture (TC)-treated surface to support optimal cell attachment, growth, and proliferation. Designed for routine cell culture applications, these dishes provide a reliable environment for cultivating a wide range of adherent cell types in research, biotechnology, and pharmaceutical laboratories.\\n\\nThe precision-engineered flat-bottom design creates a uniform growth surface, promoting even cell distribution and reducing variability caused by surface irregularities. This helps improve culture consistency, experimental reproducibility, and the accuracy of downstream analyses. The crystal-clear construction also allows excellent visibility for routine microscopic observation and cell monitoring.\\n\\nProduced under strict quality standards, BioArk cell culture dishes provide dependable performance for cell maintenance, expansion, transfection studies, and other cell-based research applications.", "imageUrl": "", "link": "/reagents/150-mm-tissue-culture-treated-cell-culture-dish-sterile", "category": "category-1780539818236", "createdAt": 1780980717391, "groupName": "Cell Culture Dishes"}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/87cd0436-5f9e-403b-8995-ce9d6d1eb723.jpg", "/media/product_images/06b3841a-d637-442a-a973-638a79b75228.jpg", "/media/product_images/33ce6789-ba0a-4fb9-998b-093f10295aaa.jpg", "/media/product_images/192d411d-cdb9-40d9-a948-049a3b74da38.jpg"], "createdAt": 1780980717391, "catalogNumber": "BA803150", "availability": "In Stock", "listPrice": "$141", "options": ["8 Packs/Case(80 Pcs/Case)"], "optionPrices": {}, "keyFeatures": ["\\u2022 Enhanced Handling and Ergonomic Design", "\\u2022 Secure and Stable Stacking for Easy Storage and Transport", "\\u2022 TC-Treated Surface for Improved Cell Attachment and Growth", "\\u2022 Suitable for Both Adherent and Suspension Cell Culture", "\\u2022 Uniform Growth Surface for Consistent Cell Distribution", "\\u2022 Excellent Optical Clarity for Microscopic Observation", "\\u2022 Ideal for Cell-Based Assays and Biological Research", "\\u2022 Reliable Performance for Routine Cell Culture Applications", "\\u2022 Durable Polystyrene Construction", "\\u2022 Sterile and Ready-to-Use"], "storageStability": "", "performanceData": "\\u2022 Supports the culture, expansion, and maintenance of adherent cells for routine research and laboratory applications.\\n\\n\\u2022 Provides a suitable environment for the growth and handling of suspension cells in biological and biomedical studies.\\n\\n\\u2022 Enables cell-based assays, including cell viability, proliferation, migration, and cytotoxicity studies.\\n\\n\\u2022 Facilitates microscopic observation, cell imaging, and morphological analysis through its optically clear design.\\n\\n\\u2022 Supports studies of cell signaling pathways, cellular responses, and cell-to-cell communication.\\n\\n\\u2022 Ideal for stem cell and primary cell culture applications requiring reliable cell attachment and growth conditions.\\n\\n\\u2022 Widely used in drug discovery, compound screening, and toxicity testing workflows.\\n\\n\\u2022 Serves as a versatile platform for biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and life science research applications.\\n\\n\\u2022 Promotes consistent and reproducible cell growth for downstream molecular and cellular analyses.", "manuals": [], "manualUrls": [], "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "showInReagentSection": false, "isFeatured": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z'),
    (66, E'custom-1780980348079', E'T175 Tissue Culture Flask, Treated Surface, Sterile', E'BioArk Cell Culture Flasks are designed to provide a reliable and efficient environment for the cultivation, expansion, and maintenance of adherent cells. Manufactured from high-quality polystyrene with a tissue culture-treated surface, these flasks offer excellent cell attachment and growth while maximizing available culture area through their optimized flat growth surface.\n\nThe ergonomic angled neck design provides easy access for pipettes and cell scrapers, simplifying media exchange and cell handling procedures. Vented caps equipped with a 0.2 μm hydrophobic filter promote efficient gas exchange while helping to protect cultures from microbial contamination, ensuring optimal conditions for cell growth. Large writing areas on each flask allow convenient sample identification and experimental tracking.\n\nProduced under stringent quality standards, BioArk Cell Culture Flasks deliver consistent performance and dependable results for routine cell culture applications. Available in T25, T75, and T175 growth areas, these flasks accommodate a wide range of research, biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and clinical laboratory workflows.', E'/media/product_images/3e1d24f1-0186-43fd-9954-9a17333e75ba.JPG', E'/reagents/t175-tissue-culture-flask-treated-surface-sterile', E'category-1780539818236', E'Cell Culture Flasks', E'product', NULL, 1780980348079, E'2026-06-08T23:45:48.079000', E'BA803175', E'In Stock', E'$165', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'• TC-Treated Surface for Enhanced Cell Attachment and Growth', E'• Vented Cap with 0.2 μm Filter for Efficient Gas Exchange and Contamination Protection', E'• Ergonomic Angled Neck for Easy Access with Pipettes and Cell Scrapers', E'• Dual-Sided Graduations and Writing Areas for Convenient Volume Monitoring and Sample Identification', E'• Individually Packaged in Sterile, Self-Sealing Bags to Maintain Product Integrity', E'• Stackable Design for Efficient Storage and Handling', E'• Gamma Sterilized and Ready-to-Use', E'• Certified DNase-Free and RNase-Free for Sensitive Cell Culture Applications', E'• High-Clarity Polystyrene Construction for Easy Visual Inspection of Cell Cultures', E'• Available in Multiple Growth Areas to Support Diverse Cell Culture Requirements']::text[], ARRAY[E'10 Packs/Case(50Pcs/Case)']::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'• Supports the culture and expansion of adherent cell lines by providing a tissue culture-treated surface that promotes strong and consistent cell attachment.\n\n• Ideal for long-term cell maintenance and routine cell propagation in research, biotechnology, and pharmaceutical laboratories.\n\n• Enables efficient large-scale cell expansion for downstream applications such as protein expression, cell banking, and assay development.\n\n• Suitable for a wide range of mammalian cell culture workflows, including transfection, gene expression studies, and cell-based assays.\n\n• Provides a reliable platform for drug discovery, toxicity testing, and other cell biology research applications requiring reproducible cell growth.', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/3e1d24f1-0186-43fd-9954-9a17333e75ba.JPG', E'/media/product_images/1a106235-99c0-4312-bdbe-134ebae1f74c.JPG', E'/media/product_images/0f02bf7d-6281-4354-b896-b59e008e5d9e.JPG']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1780980348079", "name": "T175 Tissue Culture Flask, Treated Surface, Sterile", "description": "BioArk Cell Culture Flasks are designed to provide a reliable and efficient environment for the cultivation, expansion, and maintenance of adherent cells. Manufactured from high-quality polystyrene with a tissue culture-treated surface, these flasks offer excellent cell attachment and growth while maximizing available culture area through their optimized flat growth surface.\\n\\nThe ergonomic angled neck design provides easy access for pipettes and cell scrapers, simplifying media exchange and cell handling procedures. Vented caps equipped with a 0.2 \\u03bcm hydrophobic filter promote efficient gas exchange while helping to protect cultures from microbial contamination, ensuring optimal conditions for cell growth. Large writing areas on each flask allow convenient sample identification and experimental tracking.\\n\\nProduced under stringent quality standards, BioArk Cell Culture Flasks deliver consistent performance and dependable results for routine cell culture applications. Available in T25, T75, and T175 growth areas, these flasks accommodate a wide range of research, biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and clinical laboratory workflows.", "imageUrl": "", "link": "/reagents/t175-tissue-culture-flask-treated-surface-sterile", "category": "category-1780539818236", "createdAt": 1780980348079, "groupName": "Cell Culture Flasks"}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/3e1d24f1-0186-43fd-9954-9a17333e75ba.JPG", "/media/product_images/1a106235-99c0-4312-bdbe-134ebae1f74c.JPG", "/media/product_images/0f02bf7d-6281-4354-b896-b59e008e5d9e.JPG"], "createdAt": 1780980348079, "catalogNumber": "BA803175", "availability": "In Stock", "listPrice": "$165", "options": ["10 Packs/Case(50Pcs/Case)"], "optionPrices": {}, "keyFeatures": ["\\u2022 TC-Treated Surface for Enhanced Cell Attachment and Growth", "\\u2022 Vented Cap with 0.2 \\u03bcm Filter for Efficient Gas Exchange and Contamination Protection", "\\u2022 Ergonomic Angled Neck for Easy Access with Pipettes and Cell Scrapers", "\\u2022 Dual-Sided Graduations and Writing Areas for Convenient Volume Monitoring and Sample Identification", "\\u2022 Individually Packaged in Sterile, Self-Sealing Bags to Maintain Product Integrity", "\\u2022 Stackable Design for Efficient Storage and Handling", "\\u2022 Gamma Sterilized and Ready-to-Use", "\\u2022 Certified DNase-Free and RNase-Free for Sensitive Cell Culture Applications", "\\u2022 High-Clarity Polystyrene Construction for Easy Visual Inspection of Cell Cultures", "\\u2022 Available in Multiple Growth Areas to Support Diverse Cell Culture Requirements"], "storageStability": "", "performanceData": "\\u2022 Supports the culture and expansion of adherent cell lines by providing a tissue culture-treated surface that promotes strong and consistent cell attachment.\\n\\n\\u2022 Ideal for long-term cell maintenance and routine cell propagation in research, biotechnology, and pharmaceutical laboratories.\\n\\n\\u2022 Enables efficient large-scale cell expansion for downstream applications such as protein expression, cell banking, and assay development.\\n\\n\\u2022 Suitable for a wide range of mammalian cell culture workflows, including transfection, gene expression studies, and cell-based assays.\\n\\n\\u2022 Provides a reliable platform for drug discovery, toxicity testing, and other cell biology research applications requiring reproducible cell growth.", "manuals": [], "manualUrls": [], "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "showInReagentSection": false, "isFeatured": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z'),
    (67, E'custom-1780978900701', E'8-Tube PCR Strip, 0.2 mL', E'BioArk 0.2 mL Low-Profile 8-Strip PCR Tubes are specifically designed for high-performance PCR and real-time qPCR applications, providing reliable thermal transfer and consistent amplification results. The low-profile design reduces reaction dead space and enhances thermal efficiency, making these tubes ideal for fast-cycling protocols and modern thermal cyclers.\n\nManufactured from premium medical-grade polypropylene, each tube features ultra-thin, uniform walls that enable rapid and consistent heat transfer across all wells. The included optically clear flat caps provide a secure seal to minimize sample evaporation while allowing excellent fluorescence signal transmission for real-time PCR detection.\n\nProduced in an ISO Class 8 cleanroom environment, BioArk PCR tube strips are certified free of DNase, RNase, human DNA, and PCR inhibitors, and are tested non-pyrogenic to ensure optimal purity and performance. Compatible with most standard thermal cyclers and qPCR instruments, these PCR strips provide a dependable solution for molecular biology, diagnostics, genomics, and research laboratories.', E'/media/product_images/74adb8a3-d1c8-48e3-85fd-b8d7a8255bec.webp', E'/reagents/8-tube-pcr-strip-0-2-ml', E'category-1780539818236', E'PCR Consumables', E'product', NULL, 1780978900701, E'2026-06-08T23:21:40.701000', E'BA802002', E'In Stock', E'$218', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'• Low-Profile Thin-Wall Design – 0.2 mL capacity with ultra-thin 0.2 mm walls enables rapid, uniform heat transfer for efficient thermal cycling and reproducible PCR results.', E'• Optically Clear Flat Caps – Separate transparent caps provide excellent optical clarity for real-time PCR fluorescence detection and feature writable surfaces for easy sample identification.', E'• High-Purity, Contamination-Free Manufacturing – Certified free of DNase, RNase, human DNA, PCR inhibitors, and detectable DNA contamination; tested non-pyrogenic for sensitive molecular biology applications.', E'• Secure Sealing Performance – Tight-fitting caps help minimize evaporation and reduce the risk of sample cross-contamination during PCR and qPCR workflows.', E'• Flexible Strip Configuration – Robust inter-strip connections ensure stability during handling, while allowing easy separation into customized tube configurations as needed.', E'• Consistent Amplification Performance – Precision-molded tubes provide uniform wall thickness and reliable thermal conductivity across all wells.', E'• Broad Instrument Compatibility – Compatible with most standard PCR and real-time qPCR thermal cyclers commonly used in research, diagnostic, and clinical laboratories.', E'• Cleanroom Manufactured – Produced in an ISO Class 8 cleanroom environment to ensure exceptional product quality and batch-to-batch consistency.']::text[], ARRAY[E'10 Packs/Case (1250 Strips)']::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'• PCR and Real-Time qPCR Analysis – Ideal for DNA amplification, quantitative gene expression studies, and pathogen detection assays.\n\n• Genomics and Genetic Research – Suitable for gene expression profiling, genotyping, SNP analysis, and other genomics applications.\n\n• Mutation Detection and Molecular Diagnostics – Supports mutation screening, genetic testing, and clinical diagnostic workflows requiring high sensitivity and reproducibility.\n\n• Molecular Biology and Cloning Procedures – Commonly used in cloning, plasmid analysis, DNA/RNA processing, and routine molecular biology experiments.\n\n• Next-Generation Sequencing (NGS) Sample Preparation – Ideal for nucleic acid preparation, library construction, amplification, and other pre-sequencing workflows.\n\n• Academic, Clinical, and Biotechnology Research – Widely used in research laboratories, diagnostic facilities, pharmaceutical development, and biotechnology applications.', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/74adb8a3-d1c8-48e3-85fd-b8d7a8255bec.webp', E'/media/product_images/967d303a-7e5d-4e4a-81df-5181a2fa730e.webp', E'/media/product_images/15b5485e-ae06-45a3-af4c-c4c56c5b3bd0.webp', E'/media/product_images/9e844320-ffcf-4440-a951-5d7dbc6d876a.jpg']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1780978900701", "name": "8-Tube PCR Strip, 0.2 mL", "description": "BioArk 0.2 mL Low-Profile 8-Strip PCR Tubes are specifically designed for high-performance PCR and real-time qPCR applications, providing reliable thermal transfer and consistent amplification results. The low-profile design reduces reaction dead space and enhances thermal efficiency, making these tubes ideal for fast-cycling protocols and modern thermal cyclers.\\n\\nManufactured from premium medical-grade polypropylene, each tube features ultra-thin, uniform walls that enable rapid and consistent heat transfer across all wells. The included optically clear flat caps provide a secure seal to minimize sample evaporation while allowing excellent fluorescence signal transmission for real-time PCR detection.\\n\\nProduced in an ISO Class 8 cleanroom environment, BioArk PCR tube strips are certified free of DNase, RNase, human DNA, and PCR inhibitors, and are tested non-pyrogenic to ensure optimal purity and performance. Compatible with most standard thermal cyclers and qPCR instruments, these PCR strips provide a dependable solution for molecular biology, diagnostics, genomics, and research laboratories.", "imageUrl": "", "link": "/reagents/8-tube-pcr-strip-0-2-ml", "category": "category-1780539818236", "createdAt": 1780978900701, "groupName": "PCR Consumables"}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/74adb8a3-d1c8-48e3-85fd-b8d7a8255bec.webp", "/media/product_images/967d303a-7e5d-4e4a-81df-5181a2fa730e.webp", "/media/product_images/15b5485e-ae06-45a3-af4c-c4c56c5b3bd0.webp", "/media/product_images/9e844320-ffcf-4440-a951-5d7dbc6d876a.jpg"], "createdAt": 1780978900701, "catalogNumber": "BA802002",