    (71, E'custom-1772336105290', E'DNA 1kb Ladder', E'BioArk DNA 1kb Ladder (300-10000bp) consists of 10 linear double-stranded DNA (100 bp, 250 bp, 500 bp, 750 bp, 1000 bp, 1500 bp, 2000 bp, 3000 bp, 5000 bp, 8000 bp) bands mixed with 1×DNA Loading Buffer containing blue indicator dye, and is suitable for the analysis of DNA bands in agarose gel electrophoresis. This product is ready-to-use, according to the experimental needs, directly take 5-10 μL for electrophoresis, easy to use, clear electrophoresis bands, easy to accurately determine the content of the target product DNA. The 500 bp band in the DNA Marker has a DNA concentration of 100 ng/5 μL and shows a bright band; the remaining bands have a DNA concentration of 50 ng/5 μL.', E'/media/product_images/e7893cfa-77e8-4ac2-a45c-394b30842452.png', E'/reagents/dna-1kb-ladder', E'category-1765063995229', E'', E'product', NULL, 1772336105290, E'2026-02-28T22:35:05.290000', E'BADM3363', E'In Stock', E'', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'10 linear double-stranded DNA (100 bp, 250 bp, 500 bp, 750 bp, 1000 bp, 1500 bp, 2000 bp, 3000 bp, 5000 bp, 8000 bp)']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'Ship with wet ice; Store at -20℃; valid for 24 months.', E'', E'', ARRAY[E'BADM3363 Manual', E'BADM3367 Manual']::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/209f520c-0127-4573-b6f5-fac3761b3e24.pdf']::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/e7893cfa-77e8-4ac2-a45c-394b30842452.png', E'/media/product_images/9f0e70af-7461-4c5c-9ace-264b9fe59211.png', E'/media/product_images/61477ecb-a3ff-49f0-8449-f4539d89675d.png']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1772336105290", "name": "DNA 1kb Ladder", "description": "BioArk DNA 1kb Ladder (300-10000bp) consists of 10 linear double-stranded DNA (100 bp, 250 bp, 500 bp, 750 bp, 1000 bp, 1500 bp, 2000 bp, 3000 bp, 5000 bp, 8000 bp) bands mixed with 1\\u00d7DNA Loading Buffer containing blue indicator dye, and is suitable for the analysis of DNA bands in agarose gel electrophoresis. This product is ready-to-use, according to the experimental needs, directly take 5-10 \\u03bcL for electrophoresis, easy to use, clear electrophoresis bands, easy to accurately determine the content of the target product DNA. The 500 bp band in the DNA Marker has a DNA concentration of 100 ng/5 \\u03bcL and shows a bright band; the remaining bands have a DNA concentration of 50 ng/5 \\u03bcL.", "imageUrl": "", "link": "/reagents/dna-1kb-ladder", "category": "category-1765063995229", "createdAt": 1772336105290}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/e7893cfa-77e8-4ac2-a45c-394b30842452.png", "/media/product_images/9f0e70af-7461-4c5c-9ace-264b9fe59211.png", "/media/product_images/61477ecb-a3ff-49f0-8449-f4539d89675d.png"], "createdAt": 1772336105290, "catalogNumber": "BADM3363", "availability": "In Stock", "listPrice": "", "options": [], "optionPrices": {}, "keyFeatures": ["10 linear double-stranded DNA (100 bp, 250 bp, 500 bp, 750 bp, 1000 bp, 1500 bp, 2000 bp, 3000 bp, 5000 bp, 8000 bp)"], "storageStability": "Ship with wet ice; Store at -20\\u2103; valid for 24 months.", "performanceData": "", "manuals": ["BADM3363 Manual", "BADM3367 Manual"], "manualUrls": ["/media/product_images/209f520c-0127-4573-b6f5-fac3761b3e24.pdf"], "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "showInReagentSection": false, "isFeatured": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z'),
    (72, E'custom-1781002412382', E'Pre-filled 1.5 mL Sterile CryoTubes, Triple-Code, Red Flat Cap', E'BioArk 1.5 mL External Thread Cryogenic Vials are designed for secure sample storage, reliable cryopreservation, and efficient laboratory handling. Manufactured from high-quality medical-grade polypropylene (PP), these sterile cryovials provide dependable performance for the storage and transport of biological samples, cell suspensions, nucleic acids, proteins, and other temperature-sensitive materials.\n\nEach vial features a red flat external screw cap that provides a secure seal while minimizing the risk of contamination within the sealing area. The integrated white writing panel allows clear and permanent sample identification, improving traceability and reducing reliance on adhesive labels that may deteriorate under cryogenic conditions. A self-standing base enhances stability during sample preparation, aliquoting, and routine laboratory workflows.\n\nEngineered to withstand repeated freeze-thaw cycles and demanding cryogenic storage conditions, BioArk cryogenic vials maintain their integrity throughout long-term storage and transportation. Combining secure sealing, convenient labeling, and durable construction, these vials are an ideal solution for biobanking, cell culture, molecular biology, clinical diagnostics, and life science research applications.', E'/media/product_images/1d389c17-99e6-4365-a450-90fc14ed4cce.webp', E'/reagents/pre-filled-1-5-ml-sterile-cryotubes-triple-code-red-flat-cap', E'category-1780539818236', E'Cryogenic Storage', E'product', NULL, 1781002412382, E'2026-06-09T05:53:32.382000', E'BA423132', E'In Stock', E'$1,200', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'• Integrated White Writing Area – Large marking panel enables clear handwritten labeling and improves sample traceability during storage and processing.', E'• External Thread Design – Keeps the sealing surface separate from the sample area, helping reduce contamination risks and maintain sample integrity.', E'• High-Visibility Red Screw Cap – Color-coded flat cap allows rapid sample identification and efficient organization in high-throughput laboratory environments.', E'• Self-Standing Base – Freestanding design provides enhanced stability during filling, labeling, aliquoting, and routine laboratory handling.', E'• Optimized for Cryogenic Storage – Suitable for ultra-low temperature storage and repeated freeze-thaw cycles in biobanking and research applications.', E'• Sterile and Contaminant-Free – Gamma irradiated and certified RNase-free, DNase-free, with endotoxin levels ≤ 0.005 EU/mL for sensitive biological applications.', E'• Durable Medical-Grade Polypropylene – High-strength polypropylene construction delivers excellent chemical resistance and maintains integrity under cryogenic conditions.', E'• Leak-Resistant Secure Closure – Precision external-thread cap design provides dependable sealing during storage, transport, and sample handling.', E'• Ideal for Molecular Biology and Clinical Research – Suitable for the storage of cells, DNA, RNA, proteins, and other valuable biological specimens.', E'• Bulk Packaging for Laboratory Efficiency – Supplied in convenient packaging configurations to support high-throughput sample management and inventory control.']::text[], ARRAY[E'10×10 Cryotubes/Box; 30 Boxes/Case (3000 Tubes/Case)']::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'• Cryogenic Storage of Biological Samples – Ideal for the preservation of DNA, RNA, proteins, cell pellets, microbial cultures, and other temperature-sensitive specimens.\n\n• Biobanking and Sample Archiving – Supports long-term storage, organization, and traceability of valuable research and clinical samples.\n\n• Molecular Biology and Cell Culture Research – Suitable for the storage and handling of nucleic acids, cell stocks, enzymes, and biological reagents.\n\n• Clinical and Diagnostic Laboratories – Provides secure storage and management of clinical specimens, reference materials, and diagnostic samples.\n\n• Sample Labeling and Inventory Management – Integrated writing area facilitates clear sample identification and efficient freezer organization.\n\n• Ultra-Low Temperature Storage and Transport – Designed for reliable sample protection during storage in ultra-low freezers and transportation on dry ice.\n\n• Research, Biotechnology, and Pharmaceutical Applications – Supports routine cryogenic workflows in academic, biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and life science laboratories.', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/1d389c17-99e6-4365-a450-90fc14ed4cce.webp', E'/media/product_images/08bd308f-28f7-4d7b-9bc6-e9c3c67f1fb2.webp', E'/media/product_images/6a7e60bf-99d4-425d-9906-057fb5db5394.webp', E'/media/product_images/be278a11-40d6-4d2e-a772-a7efea46c96d.webp', E'/media/product_images/1cf1e718-7bce-402b-ad65-eb79fb24977f.webp']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1781002412382", "name": "Pre-filled 1.5 mL Sterile CryoTubes, Triple-Code, Red Flat Cap", "description": "BioArk 1.5 mL External Thread Cryogenic Vials are designed for secure sample storage, reliable cryopreservation, and efficient laboratory handling. Manufactured from high-quality medical-grade polypropylene (PP), these sterile cryovials provide dependable performance for the storage and transport of biological samples, cell suspensions, nucleic acids, proteins, and other temperature-sensitive materials.\\n\\nEach vial features a red flat external screw cap that provides a secure seal while minimizing the risk of contamination within the sealing area. The integrated white writing panel allows clear and permanent sample identification, improving traceability and reducing reliance on adhesive labels that may deteriorate under cryogenic conditions. A self-standing base enhances stability during sample preparation, aliquoting, and routine laboratory workflows.\\n\\nEngineered to withstand repeated freeze-thaw cycles and demanding cryogenic storage conditions, BioArk cryogenic vials maintain their integrity throughout long-term storage and transportation. Combining secure sealing, convenient labeling, and durable construction, these vials are an ideal solution for biobanking, cell culture, molecular biology, clinical diagnostics, and life science research applications.", "imageUrl": "", "link": "/reagents/pre-filled-1-5-ml-sterile-cryotubes-triple-code-red-flat-cap", "category": "category-1780539818236", "createdAt": 1781002412382, "groupName": "Cryogenic Storage"}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/1d389c17-99e6-4365-a450-90fc14ed4cce.webp", "/media/product_images/08bd308f-28f7-4d7b-9bc6-e9c3c67f1fb2.webp", "/media/product_images/6a7e60bf-99d4-425d-9906-057fb5db5394.webp", "/media/product_images/be278a11-40d6-4d2e-a772-a7efea46c96d.webp", "/media/product_images/1cf1e718-7bce-402b-ad65-eb79fb24977f.webp"], "createdAt": 1781002412382, "catalogNumber": "BA423132", "availability": "In Stock", "listPrice": "$1,200", "options": ["10\\u00d710 Cryotubes/Box; 30 Boxes/Case (3000 Tubes/Case)"], "optionPrices": {}, "keyFeatures": ["\\u2022 Integrated White Writing Area \\u2013 Large marking panel enables clear handwritten labeling and improves sample traceability during storage and processing.", "\\u2022 External Thread Design \\u2013 Keeps the sealing surface separate from the sample area, helping reduce contamination risks and maintain sample integrity.", "\\u2022 High-Visibility Red Screw Cap \\u2013 Color-coded flat cap allows rapid sample identification and efficient organization in high-throughput laboratory environments.", "\\u2022 Self-Standing Base \\u2013 Freestanding design provides enhanced stability during filling, labeling, aliquoting, and routine laboratory handling.", "\\u2022 Optimized for Cryogenic Storage \\u2013 Suitable for ultra-low temperature storage and repeated freeze-thaw cycles in biobanking and research applications.", "\\u2022 Sterile and Contaminant-Free \\u2013 Gamma irradiated and certified RNase-free, DNase-free, with endotoxin levels \\u2264 0.005 EU/mL for sensitive biological applications.", "\\u2022 Durable Medical-Grade Polypropylene \\u2013 High-strength polypropylene construction delivers excellent chemical resistance and maintains integrity under cryogenic conditions.", "\\u2022 Leak-Resistant Secure Closure \\u2013 Precision external-thread cap design provides dependable sealing during storage, transport, and sample handling.", "\\u2022 Ideal for Molecular Biology and Clinical Research \\u2013 Suitable for the storage of cells, DNA, RNA, proteins, and other valuable biological specimens.", "\\u2022 Bulk Packaging for Laboratory Efficiency \\u2013 Supplied in convenient packaging configurations to support high-throughput sample management and inventory control."], "storageStability": "", "performanceData": "\\u2022 Cryogenic Storage of Biological Samples \\u2013 Ideal for the preservation of DNA, RNA, proteins, cell pellets, microbial cultures, and other temperature-sensitive specimens.\\n\\n\\u2022 Biobanking and Sample Archiving \\u2013 Supports long-term storage, organization, and traceability of valuable research and clinical samples.\\n\\n\\u2022 Molecular Biology and Cell Culture Research \\u2013 Suitable for the storage and handling of nucleic acids, cell stocks, enzymes, and biological reagents.\\n\\n\\u2022 Clinical and Diagnostic Laboratories \\u2013 Provides secure storage and management of clinical specimens, reference materials, and diagnostic samples.\\n\\n\\u2022 Sample Labeling and Inventory Management \\u2013 Integrated writing area facilitates clear sample identification and efficient freezer organization.\\n\\n\\u2022 Ultra-Low Temperature Storage and Transport \\u2013 Designed for reliable sample protection during storage in ultra-low freezers and transportation on dry ice.\\n\\n\\u2022 Research, Biotechnology, and Pharmaceutical Applications \\u2013 Supports routine cryogenic workflows in academic, biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and life science laboratories.", "manuals": [], "manualUrls": [], "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "showInReagentSection": false, "isFeatured": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z'),
    (73, E'custom-1780975650193', E'20 μL Universal Pipette Tips – Filtered – Low Retention', E'Filtered Low-Retention Universal Pipette Tips\n\nOur Filtered Low-Retention Universal Pipette Tips are manufactured from high-quality polypropylene (PP) to provide reliable performance, precision liquid handling, and enhanced sample protection for a wide range of laboratory workflows. Designed for both single-channel and multi-channel pipettes, these tips offer broad compatibility with most major pipette brands, including Eppendorf, Gilson, Thermo Fisher, Sartorius, Biohit, Oxford, DLAB, and other standard pipette systems.\n\nFeaturing an integrated aerosol barrier filter and low-retention surface technology, these tips help minimize the risk of cross-contamination, liquid backflow, and pipette contamination while maximizing sample recovery. The low-retention design reduces liquid adhesion, improving pipetting accuracy and consistency, particularly when working with valuable or low-volume samples.\n\nAs one of the most widely used pipette tip formats in research, clinical, and diagnostic laboratories, these universal filtered tips provide a cost-effective solution for routine liquid handling applications while maintaining high standards of quality and performance. Please note that Rainin pipettes require specially designed tips and are not compatible with standard universal pipette tips. Users of less common pipette brands are encouraged to verify compatibility prior to purchase.', E'/media/product_images/88c0cb47-475a-4fe3-a8e5-513bdab45655.webp', E'/reagents/20-l-universal-pipette-tips-filtered-low-retention', E'category-1780539818236', E'Pipette Tips', E'product', NULL, 1780975650193, E'2026-06-08T22:27:30.193000', E'BA800708', E'In Stock', E'215', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'• Low-Retention Surface for Enhanced Sample Recovery and Pipetting Accuracy', E'• Integrated Aerosol Barrier Filter Helps Prevent Cross-Contamination and Liquid Backflow', E'• Universal Compatibility with Most Major Single- and Multi-Channel Pipettes', E'• Manufactured in a Class 100,000 Cleanroom Environment', E'• Certified DNase-Free, RNase-Free, and Non-Pyrogenic', E'• Sterile and Ready-to-Use for Sensitive Laboratory Applications', E'• CE Marked and ISO 13485:2016 Certified', E'• Compliant with IVDD 98/79/EC Requirements', E'• Consistent Quality and Reliable Performance for Routine and Precision Liquid Handling', E'• Ideal for PCR, qPCR, Molecular Biology, Cell Culture, and Diagnostic Workflows']::text[], ARRAY[E'10 Racks/Box; 5 Boxes/Case (4800Tips/Case)']::text[], E'{"10 Racks/Box; 5 Boxes/Case (4800Tips/Case)": "$215"}'::jsonb, E'', E'• Accurate Liquid Transfer and Precision Pipetting\n\n• Reagent, Buffer, and Sample Preparation\n\n• PCR, qPCR, and Nucleic Acid Workflows\n\n• Sample Dispensing into Microplates, PCR Plates, and Reaction Tubes\n\n• Cell Culture and Microbiology Applications\n\n• Electrophoresis Gel Loading\n\n• ELISA and Diagnostic Assays\n\n• Supernatant Transfer and Phase Separation Procedures\n\n• High-Throughput Screening and Automated Liquid Handling\n\n• Routine Research, Clinical, and Analytical Laboratory Operations', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/88c0cb47-475a-4fe3-a8e5-513bdab45655.webp', E'/media/product_images/fab669c5-b5fe-40f6-b78e-0081057948b0.webp', E'/media/product_images/e8a4a652-98a1-4533-ba6e-d968ac979482.webp', E'/media/product_images/43162be7-3eae-4042-96d2-d17231d1f2b7.jpg', E'/media/product_images/a1c802cd-40f7-43e2-874a-0b9d2f8e5661.webp']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1780975650193", "name": "20 \\u03bcL Universal Pipette Tips \\u2013 Filtered \\u2013 Low Retention", "description": "Filtered Low-Retention Universal Pipette Tips\\n\\nOur Filtered Low-Retention Universal Pipette Tips are manufactured from high-quality polypropylene (PP) to provide reliable performance, precision liquid handling, and enhanced sample protection for a wide range of laboratory workflows. Designed for both single-channel and multi-channel pipettes, these tips offer broad compatibility with most major pipette brands, including Eppendorf, Gilson, Thermo Fisher, Sartorius, Biohit, Oxford, DLAB, and other standard pipette systems.\\n\\nFeaturing an integrated aerosol barrier filter and low-retention surface technology, these tips help minimize the risk of cross-contamination, liquid backflow, and pipette contamination while maximizing sample recovery. The low-retention design reduces liquid adhesion, improving pipetting accuracy and consistency, particularly when working with valuable or low-volume samples.\\n\\nAs one of the most widely used pipette tip formats in research, clinical, and diagnostic laboratories, these universal filtered tips provide a cost-effective solution for routine liquid handling applications while maintaining high standards of quality and performance. Please note that Rainin pipettes require specially designed tips and are not compatible with standard universal pipette tips. Users of less common pipette brands are encouraged to verify compatibility prior to purchase.", "imageUrl": "", "link": "/reagents/20-l-universal-pipette-tips-filtered-low-retention", "category": "category-1780539818236", "createdAt": 1780975650193, "groupName": "Pipette Tips"}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/88c0cb47-475a-4fe3-a8e5-513bdab45655.webp", "/media/product_images/fab669c5-b5fe-40f6-b78e-0081057948b0.webp", "/media/product_images/e8a4a652-98a1-4533-ba6e-d968ac979482.webp", "/media/product_images/43162be7-3eae-4042-96d2-d17231d1f2b7.jpg", "/media/product_images/a1c802cd-40f7-43e2-874a-0b9d2f8e5661.webp"], "createdAt": 1780975650193, "catalogNumber": "BA800708", "availability": "In Stock", "listPrice": "215", "options": ["10 Racks/Box; 5 Boxes/Case (4800Tips/Case)"], "optionPrices": {"10 Racks/Box; 5 Boxes/Case (4800Tips/Case)": "$215"}, "keyFeatures": ["\\u2022 Low-Retention Surface for Enhanced Sample Recovery and Pipetting Accuracy", "\\u2022 Integrated Aerosol Barrier Filter Helps Prevent Cross-Contamination and Liquid Backflow", "\\u2022 Universal Compatibility with Most Major Single- and Multi-Channel Pipettes", "\\u2022 Manufactured in a Class 100,000 Cleanroom Environment", "\\u2022 Certified DNase-Free, RNase-Free, and Non-Pyrogenic", "\\u2022 Sterile and Ready-to-Use for Sensitive Laboratory Applications", "\\u2022 CE Marked and ISO 13485:2016 Certified", "\\u2022 Compliant with IVDD 98/79/EC Requirements", "\\u2022 Consistent Quality and Reliable Performance for Routine and Precision Liquid Handling", "\\u2022 Ideal for PCR, qPCR, Molecular Biology, Cell Culture, and Diagnostic Workflows"], "storageStability": "", "performanceData": "\\u2022 Accurate Liquid Transfer and Precision Pipetting\\n\\n\\u2022 Reagent, Buffer, and Sample Preparation\\n\\n\\u2022 PCR, qPCR, and Nucleic Acid Workflows\\n\\n\\u2022 Sample Dispensing into Microplates, PCR Plates, and Reaction Tubes\\n\\n\\u2022 Cell Culture and Microbiology Applications\\n\\n\\u2022 Electrophoresis Gel Loading\\n\\n\\u2022 ELISA and Diagnostic Assays\\n\\n\\u2022 Supernatant Transfer and Phase Separation Procedures\\n\\n\\u2022 High-Throughput Screening and Automated Liquid Handling\\n\\n\\u2022 Routine Research, Clinical, and Analytical Laboratory Operations", "manuals": [], "manualUrls": [], "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "showInReagentSection": false, "isFeatured": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z'),
    (74, E'custom-1772243282870', E'Prestained Protein Marker 250KD (10-250KD)', E'•	The Prestained Protein Marker 250 kDa is formulated with high-purity recombinant proteins and distinct multi-color reference bands, covering a broad molecular weight range of 10–250 kDa. A green 10 kDa band and orange-red bands at 25 kDa and 70 kDa, with remaining bands in blue, provide clear orientation and accurate molecular weight estimation. This ladder requires no heating, reducing agents, or sample buffer, minimizing hands-on time and improving experimental consistency. \n•	Performance is equivalent to Thermo Scientific PageRuler™ Plus Prestained Protein Ladder (Cat. 26619), while offering comparable quality at less than half the cost, delivering exceptional value for both routine and high-throughput workflows.', E'/media/product_images/4f36cf0e-7ff2-4650-bb1e-2b550ac5bbcc.png', E'/reagents/prestained-protein-marker-250kd-10-250kd', E'category-1766675365489', E'', E'product', NULL, 1772243282870, E'2026-02-27T20:48:02.870000', E'BAPM1126', E'In Stock', E'$60', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'(~10, ~15, ~25, ~35, ~55, ~70, ~100, ~130, ~250)kDa', E'with orange-red band at 25Kda and 70 kDa, green band at 10 kD']::text[], ARRAY[E'500μL', E'2 X 500μL', E'5 X 500μL']::text[], E'{"500\\u03bcL": "$60", "2 X 500\\u03bcL": "$110", "5 X 500\\u03bcL": "$250"}'::jsonb, E'Ship with wet ice; Store at -20°C; Valid for 12 months', E'', E'', ARRAY[E'BAPM1126 Manual', E'BAPM1125 Manual']::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/f4771a52-a6ed-4c0b-a961-296a41bc73a6.pdf']::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/4f36cf0e-7ff2-4650-bb1e-2b550ac5bbcc.png', E'/media/product_images/9056dc01-a706-4ea1-a54b-7f3215f1ea8f.png', E'/media/product_images/aa5afc91-8a4c-40da-9fab-d12d4406cc39.png']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1772243282870", "name": "Prestained Protein Marker 250KD (10-250KD)", "description": "\\u2022\\tThe Prestained Protein Marker 250 kDa is formulated with high-purity recombinant proteins and distinct multi-color reference bands, covering a broad molecular weight range of 10\\u2013250 kDa. A green 10 kDa band and orange-red bands at 25 kDa and 70 kDa, with remaining bands in blue, provide clear orientation and accurate molecular weight estimation. This ladder requires no heating, reducing agents, or sample buffer, minimizing hands-on time and improving experimental consistency. \\n\\u2022\\tPerformance is equivalent to Thermo Scientific PageRuler\\u2122 Plus Prestained Protein Ladder (Cat. 26619), while offering comparable quality at less than half the cost, delivering exceptional value for both routine and high-throughput workflows.", "imageUrl": "", "link": "/reagents/prestained-protein-marker-250kd-10-250kd", "category": "category-1766675365489", "createdAt": 1772243282870}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/4f36cf0e-7ff2-4650-bb1e-2b550ac5bbcc.png", "/media/product_images/9056dc01-a706-4ea1-a54b-7f3215f1ea8f.png", "/media/product_images/aa5afc91-8a4c-40da-9fab-d12d4406cc39.png"], "createdAt": 1772243282870, "catalogNumber": "BAPM1126", "availability": "In Stock", "listPrice": "$60", "options": ["500\\u03bcL", "2 X 500\\u03bcL", "5 X 500\\u03bcL"], "optionPrices": {"500\\u03bcL": "$60", "2 X 500\\u03bcL": "$110", "5 X 500\\u03bcL": "$250"}, "keyFeatures": ["(~10, ~15, ~25, ~35, ~55, ~70, ~100, ~130, ~250)kDa", "with orange-red band at 25Kda and 70 kDa, green band at 10 kD"], "storageStability": "Ship with wet ice; Store at -20\\u00b0C; Valid for 12 months", "performanceData": "", "manuals": ["BAPM1126 Manual", "BAPM1125 Manual"], "manualUrls": ["/media/product_images/f4771a52-a6ed-4c0b-a961-296a41bc73a6.pdf"], "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "showInReagentSection": false, "isFeatured": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z'),
    (75, E'custom-1780977963735', E'50 mL Individually Wrapped Serological Pipette, Filtered', E'BioArk 50 mL Polystyrene Sterile Serological Pipettes are designed to provide accurate liquid measurement and transfer for a wide range of laboratory applications. Manufactured from high-clarity polystyrene, these disposable pipettes offer excellent visibility for precise volume reading and reliable performance in cell culture, molecular biology, microbiology, clinical diagnostics, and pharmaceutical research. Their precision-molded construction ensures consistent liquid handling and dependable results across routine laboratory workflows.\n\nEach pipette is individually wrapped and sterilized by gamma irradiation or E-beam processing to maintain sterility and support aseptic techniques. Certified RNase-free, DNase-free, and non-pyrogenic, these pipettes help minimize the risk of sample contamination, making them suitable for sensitive biological and diagnostic applications. Clear, bidirectional graduations and highly visible color-coded markings enable fast volume identification and accurate dispensing, improving workflow efficiency and user convenience.\n\nDesigned for seamless compatibility with most standard pipette controllers and pipette aids, Biofargo serological pipettes provide a convenient, cost-effective solution for daily laboratory liquid handling. Their combination of accuracy, sterility, and ease of use makes them an ideal choice for research, clinical, and industrial laboratory environments.', E'/media/product_images/0a00399c-0c48-4b01-809e-319dd38436e6.webp', E'/reagents/50-ml-individually-wrapped-serological-pipette-filtered', E'category-1780539818236', E'Serological Pipettes', E'product', NULL, 1780977963735, E'2026-06-08T23:06:03.735000', E'BA804050', E'In Stock', E'$240', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'• Sterile and Ready for Immediate Use – Individually packaged and sterilized by E-beam or gamma irradiation to ensure aseptic handling and minimize contamination risk.', E'• Precise Liquid Measurement and Transfer – Calibrated 2 mL capacity with clear, bidirectional graduations for accurate aspiration and dispensing.', E'• Premium Virgin Polystyrene Construction – Manufactured from high-clarity polystyrene for excellent transparency, reliable performance, and enhanced chemical resistance.', E'• Certified Free of Biological Contaminants – RNase-free, DNase-free, non-pyrogenic, and non-cytotoxic, making the pipettes suitable for sensitive research and diagnostic applications.', E'• Easy Volume Identification – Distinctive color-coded markings enable rapid size recognition and improve laboratory workflow efficiency.', E'• Broad Instrument Compatibility – Designed to fit most standard pipette controllers and pipette aids commonly used in research, clinical, and industrial laboratories.', E'• Single-Use Disposable Design – Eliminates cleaning requirements and helps reduce sample carryover, cross-contamination, and experimental variability.', E'• Optimized for Laboratory Workflows – Ideal for cell culture, microbiology, molecular biology, clinical diagnostics, and general liquid handling applications.']::text[], ARRAY[E'5 Packs/Case(400 Pcs/Case)']::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'• Cell Culture and Tissue Culture Workflows – Accurate transfer of culture media, buffers, reagents, and cell suspensions in routine cell-based applications.\n\n• Clinical and Diagnostic Testing – Reliable liquid handling for sample preparation, assay setup, and laboratory diagnostic procedures.\n\n• Biotechnology and Pharmaceutical Research – Suitable for drug discovery, bioprocess development, formulation studies, and other research applications.\n\n• Microbiology and Bacteriology Studies – Precise measurement and transfer of microbial cultures, growth media, and laboratory reagents.\n\n• Sample Preparation and Reagent Mixing – Efficient handling, dilution, mixing, and dispensing of biological and chemical solutions.\n\n• Molecular Biology and Life Science Research – Ideal for routine laboratory workflows involving nucleic acids, proteins, enzymes, and other biological samples.\n\n• Quality Control and Analytical Laboratories – Consistent liquid transfer for testing, validation, and quality assurance procedures across research and manufacturing environments.', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/0a00399c-0c48-4b01-809e-319dd38436e6.webp', E'/media/product_images/c6af283d-a68e-4a0c-9792-a355ac12913d.JPG', E'/media/product_images/d7bea584-9fce-42d3-9347-c219ce090dd9.JPG', E'/media/product_images/215b23bf-74d2-40cb-9763-ebaef01c2a6d.JPG']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1780977963735", "name": "50 mL Individually Wrapped Serological Pipette, Filtered", "description": "BioArk 50 mL Polystyrene Sterile Serological Pipettes are designed to provide accurate liquid measurement and transfer for a wide range of laboratory applications. Manufactured from high-clarity polystyrene, these disposable pipettes offer excellent visibility for precise volume reading and reliable performance in cell culture, molecular biology, microbiology, clinical diagnostics, and pharmaceutical research. Their precision-molded construction ensures consistent liquid handling and dependable results across routine laboratory workflows.\\n\\nEach pipette is individually wrapped and sterilized by gamma irradiation or E-beam processing to maintain sterility and support aseptic techniques. Certified RNase-free, DNase-free, and non-pyrogenic, these pipettes help minimize the risk of sample contamination, making them suitable for sensitive biological and diagnostic applications. Clear, bidirectional graduations and highly visible color-coded markings enable fast volume identification and accurate dispensing, improving workflow efficiency and user convenience.\\n\\nDesigned for seamless compatibility with most standard pipette controllers and pipette aids, Biofargo serological pipettes provide a convenient, cost-effective solution for daily laboratory liquid handling. Their combination of accuracy, sterility, and ease of use makes them an ideal choice for research, clinical, and industrial laboratory environments.", "imageUrl": "", "link": "/reagents/50-ml-individually-wrapped-serological-pipette-filtered", "category": "category-1780539818236", "createdAt": 1780977963735, "groupName": "Serological Pipettes"}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/0a00399c-0c48-4b01-809e-319dd38436e6.webp", "/media/product_images/c6af283d-a68e-4a0c-9792-a355ac12913d.JPG", "/media/product_images/d7bea584-9fce-42d3-9347-c219ce090dd9.JPG", "/media/product_images/215b23bf-74d2-40cb-9763-ebaef01c2a6d.JPG"], "createdAt": 1780977963735, "catalogNumber": "BA804050", "availability": "In Stock", "listPrice": "$240", "options": ["5 Packs/Case(400 Pcs/Case)"], "optionPrices": {}, "keyFeatures": ["\\u2022 Sterile and Ready for Immediate Use \\u2013 Individually packaged and sterilized by E-beam or gamma irradiation to ensure aseptic handling and minimize contamination risk.", "\\u2022 Precise Liquid Measurement and Transfer \\u2013 Calibrated 2 mL capacity with clear, bidirectional graduations for accurate aspiration and dispensing.", "\\u2022 Premium Virgin Polystyrene Construction \\u2013 Manufactured from high-clarity polystyrene for excellent transparency, reliable performance, and enhanced chemical resistance.", "\\u2022 Certified Free of Biological Contaminants \\u2013 RNase-free, DNase-free, non-pyrogenic, and non-cytotoxic, making the pipettes suitable for sensitive research and diagnostic applications.", "\\u2022 Easy Volume Identification \\u2013 Distinctive color-coded markings enable rapid size recognition and improve laboratory workflow efficiency.", "\\u2022 Broad Instrument Compatibility \\u2013 Designed to fit most standard pipette controllers and pipette aids commonly used in research, clinical, and industrial laboratories.", "\\u2022 Single-Use Disposable Design \\u2013 Eliminates cleaning requirements and helps reduce sample carryover, cross-contamination, and experimental variability.", "\\u2022 Optimized for Laboratory Workflows \\u2013 Ideal for cell culture, microbiology, molecular biology, clinical diagnostics, and general liquid handling applications."], "storageStability": "", "performanceData": "\\u2022 Cell Culture and Tissue Culture Workflows \\u2013 Accurate transfer of culture media, buffers, reagents, and cell suspensions in routine cell-based applications.\\n\\n\\u2022 Clinical and Diagnostic Testing \\u2013 Reliable liquid handling for sample preparation, assay setup, and laboratory diagnostic procedures.\\n\\n\\u2022 Biotechnology and Pharmaceutical Research \\u2013 Suitable for drug discovery, bioprocess development, formulation studies, and other research applications.\\n\\n\\u2022 Microbiology and Bacteriology Studies \\u2013 Precise measurement and transfer of microbial cultures, growth media, and laboratory reagents.\\n\\n\\u2022 Sample Preparation and Reagent Mixing \\u2013 Efficient handling, dilution, mixing, and dispensing of biological and chemical solutions.\\n\\n\\u2022 Molecular Biology and Life Science Research \\u2013 Ideal for routine laboratory workflows involving nucleic acids, proteins, enzymes, and other biological samples.\\n\\n\\u2022 Quality Control and Analytical Laboratories \\u2013 Consistent liquid transfer for testing, validation, and quality assurance procedures across research and manufacturing environments.", "manuals": [], "manualUrls": [], "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "showInReagentSection": false, "isFeatured": false}'::jsonb, '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z', '2026-06-19T01:30:24.896Z'),
    (76, E'custom-1780979224342', E'90 × 15 mm Sterile Petri Dish', E'BioArk 90 × 15 mm Sterile Petri Dishes are manufactured from high-quality virgin polystyrene (PS) and designed for reliable microbial culture, isolation, and observation in research, clinical, industrial, and educational laboratories. The crystal-clear construction provides excellent visibility for monitoring colony growth, morphology, and contamination, making these dishes ideal for a wide range of microbiological applications.\n\nThe precision-molded 90 mm diameter and 15 mm height design offers a standardized culture surface suitable for bacterial, fungal, and yeast cultivation. The flat growth surface promotes even distribution of culture media and samples, while the secure-fitting lid helps reduce contamination and moisture loss during incubation.\n\nSterilized by gamma irradiation and produced under strict quality control standards, BioArk Petri Dishes are ready for immediate use and provide dependable performance for routine laboratory workflows. Their disposable design eliminates the need for cleaning and re-sterilization, improving efficiency and minimizing cross-contamination risks. These dishes are widely used for microbiological testing, environmental monitoring, quality control, food safety analysis, and life science research.', E'/media/product_images/388e403b-f3f8-4bb4-9fd8-b8a38ab19b8a.jpg', E'/reagents/90-15-mm-sterile-petri-dish', E'category-1780539818236', E'Bacterial Culture plate', E'product', NULL, 1780979224342, E'2026-06-08T23:27:04.342000', E'BAAB1001', E'In Stock', E'$129', NULL, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, ARRAY[E'BioArk 90 × 15 mm Sterile Petri Dishes are manufactured from high-quality virgin polystyrene (PS) and designed for reliable microbial culture, isolation, and observation in research, clinical, industrial, and educational laboratories. The crystal-clear construction provides excellent visibility for monitoring colony growth, morphology, and contamination, making these dishes ideal for a wide range of microbiological applications.', E'The precision-molded 90 mm diameter and 15 mm height design offers a standardized culture surface suitable for bacterial, fungal, and yeast cultivation. The flat growth surface promotes even distribution of culture media and samples, while the secure-fitting lid helps reduce contamination and moisture loss during incubation.', E'Sterilized by gamma irradiation and produced under strict quality control standards, BioArk Petri Dishes are ready for immediate use and provide dependable performance for routine laboratory workflows. Their disposable design eliminates the need for cleaning and re-sterilization, improving efficiency and minimizing cross-contamination risks. These dishes are widely used for microbiological testing, environmental monitoring, quality control, food safety analysis, and life science research.']::text[], ARRAY[E'500 Pcs/Case']::text[], E'{}'::jsonb, E'', E'• Manufactured from High-Quality Virgin Polystyrene (PS)\n\n• Standard 90 × 15 mm Format for Routine Microbiological Applications\n\n• Crystal-Clear Construction for Easy Colony Observation and Analysis\n\n• Flat, Uniform Surface for Consistent Culture Growth\n\n• Secure-Fitting Lid Helps Minimize Contamination and Moisture Loss\n\n• Excellent Optical Clarity for Colony Identification and Monitoring\n\n• Gamma Irradiated and Sterile for Immediate Use\n\n• Disposable Design Eliminates Cleaning and Re-Sterilization Requirements\n\n• Lightweight, Durable, and Easy to Handle', E'', ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY[E'/media/product_images/388e403b-f3f8-4bb4-9fd8-b8a38ab19b8a.jpg', E'/media/product_images/2a1d0d35-9a76-4f5b-b22b-552406da1dba.jpg', E'/media/product_images/8a348c93-feb5-482d-9072-03fd3b3f9416.jpg', E'/media/product_images/fc0c1846-10b2-46eb-870f-e7b0eb7178fe.jpg']::text[], E'https://store.bioarktech.com/cart', E'', FALSE, E'{"id": "custom-1780979224342", "name": "90 \\u00d7 15 mm Sterile Petri Dish", "description": "BioArk 90 \\u00d7 15 mm Sterile Petri Dishes are manufactured from high-quality virgin polystyrene (PS) and designed for reliable microbial culture, isolation, and observation in research, clinical, industrial, and educational laboratories. The crystal-clear construction provides excellent visibility for monitoring colony growth, morphology, and contamination, making these dishes ideal for a wide range of microbiological applications.\\n\\nThe precision-molded 90 mm diameter and 15 mm height design offers a standardized culture surface suitable for bacterial, fungal, and yeast cultivation. The flat growth surface promotes even distribution of culture media and samples, while the secure-fitting lid helps reduce contamination and moisture loss during incubation.\\n\\nSterilized by gamma irradiation and produced under strict quality control standards, BioArk Petri Dishes are ready for immediate use and provide dependable performance for routine laboratory workflows. Their disposable design eliminates the need for cleaning and re-sterilization, improving efficiency and minimizing cross-contamination risks. These dishes are widely used for microbiological testing, environmental monitoring, quality control, food safety analysis, and life science research.", "imageUrl": "", "link": "/reagents/90-15-mm-sterile-petri-dish", "category": "category-1780539818236", "createdAt": 1780979224342, "groupName": "Bacterial Culture plate"}'::jsonb, NULL, E'{"images": ["/media/product_images/388e403b-f3f8-4bb4-9fd8-b8a38ab19b8a.jpg", "/media/product_images/2a1d0d35-9a76-4f5b-b22b-552406da1dba.jpg", "/media/product_images/8a348c93-feb5-482d-9072-03fd3b3f9416.jpg", "/media/product_images/fc0c1846-10b2-46eb-870f-e7b0eb7178fe.jpg"], "createdAt": 1780979224342, "catalogNumber": "BAAB1001", "availability": "In Stock", "listPrice": "$129", "options": ["500 Pcs/Case"], "optionPrices": {}, "keyFeatures": ["BioArk 90 \\u00d7 15 mm Sterile Petri Dishes are manufactured from high-quality virgin polystyrene (PS) and designed for reliable microbial culture, isolation, and observation in research, clinical, industrial, and educational laboratories. The crystal-clear construction provides excellent visibility for monitoring colony growth, morphology, and contamination, making these dishes ideal for a wide range of microbiological applications.", "The precision-molded 90 mm diameter and 15 mm height design offers a standardized culture surface suitable for bacterial, fungal, and yeast cultivation. The flat growth surface promotes even distribution of culture media and samples, while the secure-fitting lid helps reduce contamination and moisture loss during incubation.", "Sterilized by gamma irradiation and produced under strict quality control standards, BioArk Petri Dishes are ready for immediate use and provide dependable performance for routine laboratory workflows. Their disposable design eliminates the need for cleaning and re-sterilization, improving efficiency and minimizing cross-contamination risks. These dishes are widely used for microbiological testing, environmental monitoring, quality control, food safety analysis, and life science research."], "storageStability": "", "performanceData": "\\u2022 Manufactured from High-Quality Virgin Polystyrene (PS)\\n\\n\\u2022 Standard 90 \\u00d7 15 mm Format for Routine Microbiological Applications\\n\\n\\u2022 Crystal-Clear Construction for Easy Colony Observation and Analysis\\n\\n\\u2022 Flat, Uniform Surface for Consistent Culture Growth\\n\\n\\u2022 Secure-Fitting Lid Helps Minimize Contamination and Moisture Loss\\n\\n\\u2022 Excellent Optical Clarity for Colony Identification and Monitoring\\n\\n\\u2022 Gamma Irradiated and Sterile for Immediate Use\\n\\n\\u2022 Disposable Design Eliminates Cleaning and Re-Sterilization Requirements\\n\\n\\u2022 Lightweight, Durable, and Easy to Handle", "manuals": [], "manualUrls": [], "storeLink": "https://store.bioarktech.com/cart", "showInReagentSection": fals